{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RfjmNUmBZVfJ3h8P26pRy5","type":"tool_result","content":"1649\t| 8 | SIDE-SHIFT | cp15 − 200 m | \"Mines ahead. Side-shift with {shiftL} or {shiftR} to slip past.\" | a mine line at cp15 + 40 m (3 mines spanning 2/3 of the width, the gap on the side away from the racing line) passed with no hit and a side-shift used in the last 1.5 s |\n1650\t| 9 | BARREL ROLL | cp11 − 100 m (about 2.5 s before the lip), at 300 km/h | \"Off the Harbour Step, flick {steer} left-right, or press {shiftL}/{shiftR} in the air. Land the roll for a boost.\" | a `roll` event with `ok` |\n1651\t| 10 | PIT LANE | cp21 + 0 m, energy 40 % | \"Shield low. Ride the green pit strip to recharge to full.\" | energy ≥ 99 |\n1652\t| 11 | FULL LAP | grid, standing start | \"Put it together. One lap under sixty seconds.\" | a lap ≤ 60.0 s at SPARK (the ideal line is about 46 s) |\n1653\t\n1654\t\n1655\t**Race radio:** a pool of about 30 short lines, gibberish plus subtitle in the radio box, rate-limited to one per\n1656\t12 s. Triggers: overtaking or being overtaken by a named pilot, a weapon hit, an elimination, the final lap. Speakers\n1657\tare the pilots (§4.1 banter, plus 2 more each), for example:\n1658\t- \"Make room.\" / \"Too slow, rookie.\" / \"That one stung.\" / \"Shield's holding.\" / \"Pit lane, now.\" (own team)\n1659\t- RIVAL: \"Behind you. Still.\" / \"Smile for the wreck report.\"\n1660\t\n1661\t### 4.6 Sponsors and signage (`66-scenery.js` canvas textures)\n1662\t\n1663\tFictional brands for gantries, billboards, wall panels and holograms. Each is a logo (a geometric mark drawn in px)\n1664\tplus a name and a slogan, in the engine's pixel font at scale 2–4 on 128–256 px canvases:\n1665\t\n1666\t| Brand | Slogan |\n1667\t| --- | --- |\n1668\t| QWIK-FUEL | FILL UP. FALL UP. |\n1669\t| OKTA NOODLE | EAT AT 600 KM/H |\n1670\t| HALCYON BANK | YOUR MONEY, FASTER |\n1671\t| AXON AIR | BREATHE PREMIUM |\n1672\t| VANTA PAINTS | DARKER THAN NOTHING |\n1673\t| MERIDIAN TELECOM | ALWAYS ON. ALWAYS. |\n1674\t| POLARIS COLD STORAGE | WE KEEP IT FROM YOU |\n1675\t| NOVA-CHROME | SHINE RESPONSIBLY |\n1676\t| KIBO TEA | STEEPED IN THE FUTURE |\n1677\t| ORBIT SOCKS | KEEP YOUR FEET IN ORBIT |\n1678\t| THE AUTHORITY | DO NOT LOOK DIRECTLY AT THE FUTURE |\n1679\t| SOLENNE TOURISM | COME FOR THE SEA. STAY FOR THE SPEED. |\n1680\t\n1681\tSignage: SECTOR markers 1–8, PIT, the jump warnings (\"GORGE: 270 KM/H MINIMUM\"), and chevron boards.\n1682\t\n1683\t---\n1684\t\n1685\t## 5. Build order and milestones\n1686\t\n1687\tThe ordering principle: **the riskiest unknown first**. First the 3D stack in one file, then the core loop (one craft\n1688\ton one track), then a full race (AI and weapons). Breadth comes after that (modes, UI, season, audio), then\n1689\tintegration (attract, dev, hub). Polish is last. Each milestone ends with its tests passing in `node tests/run.mjs`.\n1690\t\n1691\t| # | Milestone | Deliverables | Exit tests (all automated unless marked 📷 = screenshot review) |\n1692\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1693\t| **M0** | Skeleton and stack spike | Dev folder, pinned downloads (§2.1), `package.json`, `tests/run.mjs` and `tests/lib/vm.mjs`, `tools/bundle.mjs`, `index.html`. A minimal `95-main.js`: `new E.Game` with SN.INPUT, the boot steps (the 3D wait/init), a test oval TrackDef rendered as a plain ribbon mesh in a terrain world, a dummy craft box moving along it at 2000 u/s, the chase cam, an overlay text | Node: the game boots headless and `advance(5)` runs with no errors. Browser: the bundle opens from file:// with no page errors; `World3D.backend` is 'WebGPU' or 'WebGL 2'; the #view canvas is non-black over > 30 % of its area; it reaches race view in < 15 s. 📷 the ribbon and box |\n1694\t| **M1** | Tracks | `20-track.js` complete: spline, slices, frames, bank, features, surface, locate, query, line, speed profile, validation, minimap. `07-data-tracks.js` with all 4 tracks. `tools/trackcheck.mjs` | unit: frame handedness (8 headings), bank sign, closure continuity (`C(L−ε) ≈ C(0)`), arc-length error < 0.1 %, lengths within 1 % of §4.3, overpass clearances (24.5 / 31.9 m ±0.5), the `{cp,d}` feature s-values, the racing line inside the bounds, speed profile ≤ top. 📷 an overhead debug render of each track with features |\n1695\t| **M2** | One craft that flies right | `25-ship.js`, `27-collide.js` (bodies only), `01-input.js` (mapping, double tap, flick, vpad), Tune registry, engine edits §2.7.1–3 (glyphs default, font glyphs, analog values) and §2.7.5. A player craft on any track, keyboard and pad | physics suite (§7.2): the feel targets of §3.2, walls never crossed at 3000 u/s, no NaN in 10 min of random input, the jumps per App. C at each class, drop landings, overpass stability (s never jumps levels), pads, pit, side-shift lateral 3–5 m, the barrel-roll boost and botch, rescue after a fall, a simple line bot (`T.line` + `T.vline` with PD steering) laps every track × class with 0 rescues |\n1696\t| **M3** | It looks like the game | `60-render.js` (worlds, interpolation, cameras), `64-trackmesh.js` (surface, walls with neon and chevrons, pads, tunnels, supports, gantries, drop and gap faces), `62-shipkit.js` (6 craft, liveries, flaps, glow, trails, roll), the themes' sky/fog/sun and terrain carve, basic scenery per theme, bloom | browser: each track loads in < 10 s; no shader stalls over 50 ms after GO (frame-time log); 📷 per track: the start grid, a banked corner (roll sign), a tunnel, the jump, the overpass from both decks; all 6 craft on the turntable |\n1697\t| **M4** | A real race | `40-race.js` (lifecycle, grid, countdown and launch revs, laps, sectors, positions, wrong way, finish, results, elimination), `35-ai.js` (line, speed, control, avoidance, pads, mistakes, rubber band, difficulty), `45-replay.js` (record and replay, hash) | race suite: an 8-AI race on every track × class finishes; no craft stuck > 3 s; ≤ 1 rescue per craft per race; lap times within ±25 % of §4.2; positions consistent with progress; `hash` equal on two runs from the same seed; a replay re-sim gives an equal hash; wrong-way detection; the launch-boost window |\n1698\t| **M5** | Combat | `30-weapons.js` (pads, roll table, 10 weapons, absorb, lock-on, damage, stagger), AI weapon logic, `68-fx.js` for every weapon, events wired to interim SFX (`audio.define` voices; M9 replaces every one, and none may remain) | weapons suite: each weapon fired by a scripted craft at a target in a fixed setup deals its damage; the target's warning appears; BULWARK blocks; absorb adds energy; MINEFIELD triggers; TREMOR misses airborne craft; SIPHON transfers; RAILSHOT hits within its aim tolerance and misses outside; elimination at 0 (DNF in a race, respawn in SNIPEOUT); in an 8-AI race every weapon is used at least once across 4 seeded races |\n1699\t| **M6** | HUD and front-end | `70-hud.js`, `55-glyphs.js`, `75-ui.js` (widget kit, every §3.9 screen), settings (§3.17), pause items, the touch-only notice, the About skeleton | flow suite: title → menu → quick race setup → loading → race → results → menu by scripted taps; mouse hover focus (`input.feed('move')`) and click activation; the prompt bar switches device (key, pad stub, mouse); Button symbols switches PS ↔ Xbox labels; the touch-only notice when `matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)')` is false and `maxTouchPoints > 0` (stubbed in vm), with no touch buttons (`input.touchButtons` never called). 📷 every screen at 1280×720 and 1920×1080 |\n1700\t| **M7** | Every mode | TIME TRIAL plus ghosts, HOT LAP, SNIPEOUT, OVERCLOCK plus the skin, ACADEMY (11 drills, drone, gates, mine line), VERSUS (join, half keys, split HUD), the REPLAY scene, records | modes suite: each mode starts, plays, and ends with correct results; ghost save/load round-trips and plays back aligned (< 1 m error); Overclock zones advance and the run ends at 0 energy; the academy bot passes all drills; versus with 2 inputs makes 2 viewports and both finish; replay click-to-follow selects the clicked craft (feed a click at a projected position) |\n1701\t| **M8** | Season and story | `08-data-season.js`, `09-data-story.js`, `78-season-ui.js` (hub, briefings, GP, ending, credits), saves, unlocks | season suite: the **scripted playthrough** (§7.4) of the whole season with the player bot; unlocks fire in order; save → reload → state equal; every dialog line references only defined vars; every event playable |\n1702\t| **M9** | Sound | engine edit §2.7.4; `50-audio.js`: 6 songs and stings, the full SFX catalogue, engine hums, the music director (layers, final lap, overclock tempo), `SN.Voice` gibberish, announcer callouts, radio | audio suite (headless, no WebAudio): every song parses with no engine warnings and is ≥ 16 bars; each event type maps to an existing sound; `Voice.say` durations are > 0 and stable per word; the music layers react to race events (`audio.pos.layers`). 🔊 a human-free check: in the browser, record `audio.drift` stays < 10 ms and no audio errors |\n1703\t| **M10** | Attract and dev | `85-attract.js`, `80-dev.js` (panel, cheats, sliders, reset, overlays, info) | flow: 10.0 s idle on the title → attract starts (not at 9.9 s); any of key/pad/click exits within 1 step; the attract shows ≥ 8 distinct weapons and ≥ 3 tracks across one loop (counted from events); dev: every slider changes `SN.Tune.T` and the sim responds (e.g., topSpeedMul 1.5 raises top speed); RESET ALL restores every default exactly; each cheat works |\n1704\t| **M11** | AI Hub | `90-hub.js`, its own card, ghost send/receive, the session scene | hub suite (Node mock of `AIHub`, §7.6) and the **real harness** (§7.6): `players=2&auto=1`, `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, `…&scenario=host-leave`; `__hubCheck.pass === true` in each |\n1705\t| **M12** | Polish and ship | scenery density, effects, juice (shake, flashes, rumble via `input.rumble`), the balance pass with the sliders, medal calibration (`tools/medals.mjs`), the About pages filled, `exit-interview.json`, the final bundle | the full `node tests/run.mjs` passes; `tools/bundle.mjs` passes its checks (no TODO, an identical hub client); `node engine/handoff/tools/check.mjs ../<bundle>.html` gives no errors (it will list the CDN files as external, which is expected); 📷 the final screenshot set (§7.7) |\n1706\t\n1707\t**The vertical slice at the end of M5** must already *play* like the game: a full race with AI and weapons on every\n1708\ttrack. If time runs short later, the plan's priorities hold:\n1709\t1. a feature's existence and correctness (§8);\n1710\t2. the playthrough test;\n1711\t3. the look;\n1712\t4. the quantity of content.\n1713\t\n1714\t---\n1715\t\n1716\t## 6. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1717\t\n1718\t| # | Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk (when) |\n1719\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1720\t| 1 | **The 3D stack in one file** (an inline ES module, an import map to the CDN, file://, WebGPU → WebGL 2 fallback, headless Chromium) | Nothing else works if it doesn't. It is new to most builders | **M0 spike first.** Prove the bundle from file:// in Playwright with a picture. If the CDN is blocked in the test environment, retry once, then vendor `three.webgpu.min.js`, `three.core.min.js` (imported by it), `three.tsl.min.js` and `rapier.mjs` as inline modules: rewrite the import map to `data:`/blob URLs made by a tiny classic loader, or inline the files as `<script type=\"module\">` with the specifiers mapped to blob URLs. Keep the CDN as the default (smaller file) |\n1721\t| 2 | **Frame and handedness bugs** (a left-handed engine frame, bank signs, camera roll sign, `toThree`) | Silent wrongness: mirrored steering, banks the wrong way, a camera rolling backwards | Unit tests in M1 (§7.2) before any physics. One `SN.frame` helper, used everywhere. A screenshot check of the roll on the Karakum spiral (M3) |\n1722\t| 3 | **Physics at 3,000 u/s** (tunnelling, jitter on crests, stuck on walls, overpasses confusing the track lookup) | The core feel. Hard to see in code review | Track-space walls are analytic (no tunnelling). Local-only `locate`. Invariant tests over long random-input runs (M2). Dev sliders for live tuning. The App. C jump numbers become tests |\n1723\t| 4 | **AI that finishes on every track** (the jump speeds, hairpins, overpass, open edges, the drop in a curve) | A stuck AI breaks races, attract, the season playthrough and medal calibration | One line/profile generator plus a PD controller, tested on 4 tracks × 4 classes × 4 seeds in M4. A stuck detector, rescue, and a per-track min-speed constraint at the gap |\n1724\t| 5 | **Determinism** (replays, the hub's fair start, hashes) | Any `Math.random`, dt or order dependence breaks replays | §2.8 rules. A lint test that greps the sim files for `Math.random`, `Date.now` and `performance.now`. Hash-equality tests from M4 on |\n1725\t| 6 | **Shader stalls and loading hitches** (World3D compiles on first use) | Visible hitches at GO or on the first weapon | Materials only at world creation. The warm-up frame and `world.prepare()` in loading (§3.7). Frame-time logging in the M3 browser test |\n1726\t| 7 | **Scope** (11 modes, 4 tracks, season, audio, hub) | Running out of time with stubs left (the brief forbids stubs) | Milestone order puts every feature in a minimal complete form before polish. The §8 checklist is the definition of done. Cut quantity, never features |\n1727\t| 8 | **Hub conformance** (card, ready without keys, time-up, end, ghosts) | The hub keeps failing games out of sessions | The Node mock early (M11 start), then the real harness at 1, 2 and 4 players with network faults and host-leave. The session path shares the race code, so it adds little new code |\n1728\t| 9 | **Synth music quality** | Bad music undermines the source's identity | The engine edits (filter env, unison) make house/acid/trance timbres possible. Compose at least 16 bars with A/B sections and use layers. A headless check that songs parse. A listen in the browser (the builder has no ears, so check with `audio.pos` and drift) |\n1729\t| 10 | **Readability at 10 feet** (a 427×240 HUD on a TV) | Tiny text is the default trap | HUD at scale 2 minimum for numbers, the large-HUD option, ≤ 6 items per screen. Screenshots at 1920×1080 scaled down to 50 % must stay legible (📷 M6) |\n1730\t| 11 | **Analog triggers and DualSense mapping** | The engine reads only `pressed` | Engine edit §2.7.3, tested with a stubbed `navigator.getGamepads()` in Playwright (axes and button `value`) |\n1731\t| 12 | **/tmp nearly full** (a shared tmpfs) | Playwright and Chromium need temp space | `TMPDIR=<dev>/.tmp` for every tool run (§0) |\n1732\t| 13 | **Terrain intersecting the track or tunnels** | The ground poking through decks or tunnel interiors looks broken | The corridor grid carve (§3.7) plus portal frames. 📷 every tunnel portal and every elevated section in M3 |\n1733\t\n1734\t---\n1735\t\n1736\t## 7. Testing (one command)\n1737\t\n1738\t**The command:** `cd SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174728 && TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp node tests/run.mjs`.\n1739\tIt runs every suite (Node first, then browser, then the hub harness). It prints **only failures** (suite › test:\n1740\tmessage, plus the snapshot JSON where useful) and **one final line**:\n1741\t`412 passed, 0 failed (node 380, browser 22, hub 10) in 96 s`.\n1742\t- `node tests/run.mjs physics race` runs only the named suites.\n1743\t- `--node` skips the browser and hub suites.\n1744\t- Rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers (the suites map to files, listed in `tests/run.mjs`).\n1745\t\n1746\t### 7.1 Harness\n1747\t\n1748\t`tests/lib/vm.mjs` follows the handoff's `game/test.mjs` and `kits/test.mjs`:\n1749\t- a `vm` context with stand-ins `window = ctx`, `addEventListener() {}`, `location: { search: '', hash: '' }`,\n1750\t  `matchMedia`, `navigator: { maxTouchPoints: 0, getGamepads: () => [] }`;\n1751\t- it runs `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, then the `src/` files in manifest order;\n1752\t- `E.current` is the game, and `game.advance(s)` drives it;\n1753\t- scripted input through `game.input.tap/hold/press`, `input.feed` for the mouse, and `SN.vpad` for analog;\n1754\t- assertions through `game.debug.snapshot()`.\n1755\t\n1756\t```js\n1757\tgame.debug = {\n1758\t  snapshot: () => ({ scene, state, mode, track, cls, t, ships: [{ id, p, s, u, h, v, kmh, energy, lap, place, weapon, airborne, finished, elim }],\n1759\t                     player: {...}, hudCallouts: [...], focus: ui.focusId, device: input.lastDevice, attract: bool, dev: bool,\n1760\t                     season: { medals, unlocked }, hub: { connected, sent, progressCount } }),\n1761\t  teleport(s, u = 0, v = 0), give(weapon), setEnergy(x), finishNow(), events: () => race.events.slice(),\n1762\t  race: () => race, track: () => track, tune: SN.Tune\n1763\t};\n1764\t```\n1765\t\n1766\t### 7.2 Node suites (fast, about 60 s in all)\n1767\t\n1768\t- **unit:**\n1769\t  - math and frames (8 headings), bank sign, `toThree` mapping;\n1770\t  - the spline: closure, arc length, knot s;\n1771\t  - each TrackDef validates;\n1772\t  - feature s-values; `query` returns the right deck at overpasses;\n1773\t  - the racing line inside the bounds; speed profile ≤ top;\n1774\t  - Tune def/reset;\n1775\t  - the input mapping: double-tap, flick, ramped keys;\n1776\t  - the hash is stable;\n1777\t  - **lint:** the sim files contain no `Math.random`, `Date.now`, `performance.now`, `alert(`, `confirm(`, `prompt(`\n1778\t    or `window.open`, and no file contains TODO.\n1779\t- **physics:**\n1780\t  - every feel target in §3.2;\n1781\t  - jumps: Karakum's gap at 70 / 80 / 90 / 140 m/s (fails at 70, clears at ≥ 80, landing window as App. C ±15 %), drops\n1782\t    land at 45 and 170 m/s;\n1783\t  - long random-input soak (10 simulated minutes, 4 tracks): no NaN, never `|u| > hw` on walled decks, never `h < 0`;\n1784\t  - overpass: a craft on the upper deck stays on it (its s stays in the upper range);\n1785\t  - pads, pit recharge, side-shift, roll ok/botch, rescue after an open-edge fall;\n1786\t  - launch boost window.\n1787\t- **race:**\n1788\t  - 4 tracks × 4 classes × 2 seeds of 8 AI: all finish, no stuck, rescues ≤ 1 per craft, lap times within ±25 % of\n1789\t    §4.2;\n1790\t  - positions sorted by progress; wrong way; final-lap event; results;\n1791\t  - determinism (2 runs, equal hash); replay re-sim equals the hash.\n1792\t- **weapons:** every row of §3.4, each in a fixed two-craft setup, plus AI usage counts.\n1793\t- **modes:** time trial (+ ghost round trip), hot lap (flying start, best lap), snipeout (scoring, respawn, the target\n1794\t  ends it), overclock (zones, tempo events, end), academy (the bot passes 11 drills), versus (2 viewports, half-keys\n1795\t  labels), grand prix (points table, ties).\n1796\t- **flow:**\n1797\t  - title → menu → setup → race → results → replay → menu;\n1798\t  - pause menu items present (Restart, Camera, How to play, Dev mode, Quit) and absent in a session;\n1799\t  - settings keys exist;\n1800\t  - glyph labels per device and setting;\n1801\t  - touch-only notice;\n1802\t  - attract timing and exit;\n1803\t  - dev sliders and reset; each cheat.\n1804\t- **season:** §7.4.\n1805\t- **audio:** song parsing, event → sound map, `Voice` durations, the music director's layer changes (headless:\n1806\t  `audio.pos`).\n1807\t- **hub (mock):** §7.6.\n1808\t\n1809\t### 7.3 The player bot (`tests/lib/bot.mjs`)\n1810\t\n1811\t`bot.drive(playerIndex, { skill: 1, weapons: true, rolls: true })`. Each step it computes `SN.AI.controls(ship, race)`\n1812\tfor the human's craft and writes them into `SN.vpad[i]`. Edge actions (fire, absorb, side-shift) go through\n1813\t`input.tap`, so the human path (mapping, double-tap, flick) is exercised. `bot.menu(path)` navigates screens by\n1814\twidget id: it taps the arrows to reach the focus, then confirm.\n1815\t\n1816\t### 7.4 Scripted playthrough of the whole game (the season suite and the `playthrough` test)\n1817\t\n1818\tOne test plays the game end to end, headless, on fixed seeds, asserting along the way:\n1819\t1. Boot → title.\n1820\t2. Wait 10 s → attract (assert it is running, weapons seen, at least 2 tracks across the playlist with\n1821\t   `game.advance(120)`) → a key press → title.\n1822\t3. → menu → ACADEMY (the bot passes the drills) → SEASON: prologue → E1…E10 in order, each via the season hub, bot\n1823\t   driving, ≥ bronze (retry up to 3 times, asserting progress), the briefings advanced by taps.\n1824\t4. Promotions unlock FLARE and STORM.\n1825\t5. GP: 4 races; assert the points and the standings screen.\n1826\t6. The ending lines and the credits play; SINGULARITY is unlocked.\n1827\t7. Then QUICK RACE at SINGULARITY on Borealis; TIME TRIAL Karakum (a ghost saved, then loaded on the next run); HOT\n1828\t   LAP Meridian; SNIPEOUT Solenne; OVERCLOCK to zone 10; VERSUS with `game.addPlayer({ keys: 'right' })` and two\n1829\t   bots; REPLAY of the last race (hash equal).\n1830\t8. The pause menu → Dev mode → slider → reset → close; Settings → Button symbols → Xbox (labels change); About pages\n1831\t   1–5.\n1832\t9. `game.errors.length === 0` throughout.\n1833\t\n1834\t### 7.5 Browser suites (Playwright, Chromium headless; `tests/browser/`)\n1835\t\n1836\t- `bundle loads`: file:// URL; no `pageerror`; `My3D2dge.World3D.backend` is set; the boot completes in < 20 s.\n1837\t- `renders`: in the race, sample the `#view` canvas (`toDataURL` or a screenshot) and require at least 40 % non-black\n1838\t  pixels and > 24 distinct colours; the HUD canvas is drawn.\n1839\t- `input devices`:\n1840\t  - keyboard thrust raises the speed;\n1841\t  - stubbed `navigator.getGamepads()` (a DualSense-like id, standard mapping): ✕ thrust, L2 `value: .5` halves the\n1842\t    airbrake, and prompts show ✕/□/○ glyphs;\n1843\t  - the Xbox setting shows A/X/B;\n1844\t  - the mouse hovers and clicks a menu tile.\n1845\t- `screens`: the flow through the menus with screenshots to `tests/out/` (📷 reviewed by the builder only for look:\n1846\t  layout, legibility, art).\n1847\t- `split screen`: 2 viewports draw two different camera poses (the pixels differ between the halves).\n1848\t- `touch-only`: emulate a phone (`hasTouch`, coarse pointer, no keyboard events) → the notice and the SETTINGS button\n1849\t  are visible, and no engine touch buttons are drawn; after 10 s the attract runs.\n1850\t- **Performance is out of scope** (TASK.md), but log the median frame time per track to `tests/out/perf.json` for\n1851\t  information.\n1852\t\n1853\t### 7.6 AI Hub tests\n1854\t\n1855\t- **Node mock** (`tests/hub/mock.mjs`): a fake `AIHub` installed before the game's scripts (`active: true`, `connect`\n1856\t  resolves `info` for seat 1 of 2, events delivered by the test). It asserts:\n1857\t  - no title or menu scenes are entered;\n1858\t  - `ready()` is called exactly once with no input;\n1859\t  - nothing moves before `start`;\n1860\t  - the race begins at `time() ≥ 0`;\n1861\t  - `progress` is called ≥ once a second, with a numeric score and a label;\n1862\t  - `send` is ≤ 20/s, unreliable, ≤ 16 KB;\n1863\t  - an incoming message creates and moves a ghost;\n1864\t  - `leave` removes it;\n1865\t  - `result({ time })` on finish (bot);\n1866\t  - `time-up` before the finish → `result({ score })` once;\n1867\t  - `end` → input ignored, music stopped, no further `send`;\n1868\t  - `card` events: Enter → `answer('ready')`, △ → `answer('more')`.\n1869\t- **Real harness** (`tests/hub/hub.test.mjs`):\n1870\t  1. Copy the bundle into a scratch dir inside `tests/out/hub/` with the pinned `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and\n1871\t     `round.js`.\n1872\t  2. Spawn `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` there (`-u`: unbuffered, so the \"Serving HTTP on 127.0.0.1\n1873\t     port N\" line arrives at once), and parse the port from it.\n1874\t  3. Fetch `/<bundle>.html` and confirm its `<title>` is `Snipeout HD` (it is our page).\n1875\t  4. Open `harness.html?game=<bundle>.html&players=2&auto=1` in Playwright, wait for `body[data-complete=\"true\"]`\n1876\t     (timeout 240 s), and read `window.__hubCheck`. Require `pass === true`, and print the failed checks otherwise.\n1877\t  5. Repeat with `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, and with `&scenario=host-leave`.\n1878\t  6. Kill the server **by its PID** (the child process you spawned).\n1879\t\n1880\t### 7.7 Screenshots (only for what scripts can't judge)\n1881\t\n1882\tPer track:\n1883\t- grid at the countdown;\n1884\t- chase cam mid-corner (bank and roll);\n1885\t- cockpit;\n1886\t- tunnel;\n1887\t- jump in flight;\n1888\t- overpass from below and above (Karakum, Meridian);\n1889\t- a weapon effect (each weapon once across tracks);\n1890\t- the Overclock skin at zone 1 and zone 20;\n1891\t- split screen.\n1892\t\n1893\tScreens: title, attract with DEMO, every menu screen, team select (each craft), results with podium, the season hub,\n1894\ta briefing with portrait, the dev panel (each tab), About pages, the touch-only notice, the hub card.\n1895\t\n1896\tReview them for: legibility at 10 feet (view at 50 %), contrast, colour-only information, a HUD clear of the corner,\n1897\tnothing clipped at 4:3, 16:9 or 21:9 (`expand: true` sizes: 1024×768, 1280×720, 2560×1080).\n1898\t\n1899\t---\n1900\t\n1901\t## 8. Definition of done: every TASK.md requirement, where it lives, how it is proven\n1902\t\n1903\t| TASK.md requirement | Where in the game | Proof |\n1904\t| --- | --- | --- |\n1905\t| Genre and perspective that fit the source | anti-gravity combat racing; chase, far and cockpit cams plus TV cameras (§1, §3.6) | 📷 M3 |\n1906\t| Title: a riff picked by a real RNG | **Snipeout HD** (§0, `secrets.randbelow`) | — |\n1907\t| One HTML file named `SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174728.html` (CDN dependencies allowed) | `tools/bundle.mjs` (§2.3) | browser: bundle loads |\n1908\t| Dev files in the subfolder; bundle in the root | §2.2 | — |\n1909\t| Built on the handoff; engine changes allowed | §2.1, §2.7 (marked edits) | About → engine changes |\n1910\t| Art: the engine's native style plus new assets that feel like the source | pixel-res World3D, toon/lambert, pixel HUD/fonts; new craft, tracks, neon, sponsors (§3.7, §4) | 📷 |\n1911\t| Animation: the engine's system plus new animations | rigs (cards, poses `cheer` / `wave` / `hips`, portraits that talk), tweens/scripts; new procedural craft animation (roll, flaps, glow, trails, barrel roll, explosions, drone), HUD/menu tweens (§3.7, §3.8) | 📷 |\n1912\t| Audio all in code; gibberish voices | the synth plus edits, 6 songs, SFX, hums, `SN.Voice` (§3.10) | audio suite |\n1913\t| Online: AI Hub integration, and multiplayer for the game on its own | ghost-mode sessions (§3.16); local 2P split-screen VERSUS | hub mock + real harness; versus test |\n1914\t| Feature-complete demo, long enough to show every mechanic | 11 modes, the season with a GP and an ending, the academy (§1, §3.3, §4.5) | the playthrough §7.4 |\n1915\t| Dev mode from the pause menu; live sliders and reset | §3.15 | flow: dev |\n1916\t| Attract mode: 10 s idle, AI demo, any input exits, may cheat | §3.14 | flow: attract |\n1917\t| Narrative tone like the source | §3.11, §4.5 | review |\n1918\t| 10-foot, controller-first, DualSense standard mapping | §3.9; analog triggers (§2.7.3) | browser: input devices |\n1919\t| Keyboard native, PC keys; mouse aims, looks, clicks; hover moves focus | §1 controls; mouse menus, fire/absorb, click-to-follow in replays, drag-rotate in team select | flow + browser |\n1920\t| Prompts follow the last device; PlayStation default; Settings option for Xbox | `55-glyphs.js`; `glyphs` default and option in Settings (§2.7.1) | flow + browser |\n1921\t| No dense web-style data screens | ≤ 6 items, big type, one row per craft (§3.9) | 📷 |\n1922\t| Touch-only: no touch controls, \"Controller or keyboard required\" plus a settings button, attract runs | §3.9 / §3.14 | browser: touch-only |\n1923\t| No TODOs, placeholders, stubs | bundle lint, unit lint (§2.3, §7.2) | tests |\n1924\t| Testing: headless scripts, `game.advance` / `game.debug`, a scripted whole-game playthrough, one command, failures only plus a one-line count | §7 | `node tests/run.mjs` |\n1925\t| Servers on 127.0.0.1 port 0, our page confirmed, stopped by PID | §7.6 | hub test |\n1926\t| Source Information, Testing/Engine/Prompt Feedback in the chat reply **and** the About/Credits screen | §3.18 | About pages; reply |\n1927\t| `exit-interview.json` in the exact shape, parses | `tools/exit-interview.mjs` (§3.18) | the script checks `JSON.parse` |\n1928\t\n1929\t---\n1930\t\n1931\t## Appendix A: reference code (use as is)\n1932\t\n1933\t**Centripetal Catmull-Rom (closed) and the arc-length resample.** This is the code the planning checker used. The §4.3\n1934\tnumbers come from it.\n1935\t\n1936\t```js\n1937\t// P: [[x, y, z], ...] closed loop; returns dense samples [[x, y, z, segIndex], ...] (k per segment)\n1938\tfunction catmullClosed(P, k = 64) {\n1939\t  const n = P.length, out = [], d = (a, b) => Math.hypot(b[0] - a[0], b[1] - a[1], b[2] - a[2]);\n1940\t  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n1941\t    const p0 = P[(i - 1 + n) % n], p1 = P[i], p2 = P[(i + 1) % n], p3 = P[(i + 2) % n];\n1942\t    const t0 = 0, t1 = Math.sqrt(d(p0, p1)), t2 = t1 + Math.sqrt(d(p1, p2)), t3 = t2 + Math.sqrt(d(p2, p3));   // alpha 0.5\n1943\t    for (let j = 0; j < k; j++) {\n1944\t      const t = t1 + (t2 - t1) * j / k, q = [];\n1945\t      for (let c = 0; c < 3; c++) {\n1946\t        const A1 = (t1 - t) / (t1 - t0) * p0[c] + (t - t0) / (t1 - t0) * p1[c];\n1947\t        const A2 = (t2 - t) / (t2 - t1) * p1[c] + (t - t1) / (t2 - t1) * p2[c];\n1948\t        const A3 = (t3 - t) / (t3 - t2) * p2[c] + (t - t2) / (t3 - t2) * p3[c];\n1949\t        const B1 = (t2 - t) / (t2 - t0) * A1 + (t - t0) / (t2 - t0) * A2;\n1950\t        const B2 = (t3 - t) / (t3 - t1) * A2 + (t - t1) / (t3 - t1) * A3;\n1951\t        q.push((t2 - t) / (t2 - t1) * B1 + (t - t1) / (t2 - t1) * B2);\n1952\t      }\n1953\t      out.push([q[0], q[1], q[2], i]);                 // (j === 0: exactly control point i: its knot)\n1954\t    }\n1955\t  }\n1956\t  return out;\n1957\t}\n1958\t// resample at a fixed spacing ds; returns { L, ds, pts, knots } (knots[i] = s of control point i)\n1959\tfunction resampleClosed(dense, ds) {\n1960\t  const n = dense.length, acc = [0], knots = [];\n1961\t  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) { const a = dense[i - 1], b = dense[i % n]; acc.push(acc[i - 1] + Math.hypot(b[0] - a[0], b[1] - a[1], b[2] - a[2])); }\n1962\t  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) if (i === 0 || dense[i][3] !== dense[i - 1][3]) knots[dense[i][3]] = acc[i];\n1963\t  const L = acc[n], m = Math.round(L / ds), step = L / m, pts = [];\n1964\t  for (let k = 0, j = 0; k < m; k++) {\n1965\t    const s = k * step; while (acc[j + 1] < s) j++;\n1966\t    const a = dense[j], b = dense[(j + 1) % n], f = (s - acc[j]) / (acc[j + 1] - acc[j]);\n1967\t    pts.push([a[0] + (b[0] - a[0]) * f, a[1] + (b[1] - a[1]) * f, a[2] + (b[2] - a[2]) * f]);\n1968\t  }\n1969\t  return { L, ds: step, pts, knots };\n1970\t}\n1971\t```\n1972\t\n1973\t**Frame helper (engine axes, left-handed: right = cross(up, forward)):**\n1974\t\n1975\t```js\n1976\tconst cross = (a, b) => [a[1] * b[2] - a[2] * b[1], a[2] * b[0] - a[0] * b[2], a[0] * b[1] - a[1] * b[0]];\n1977\tconst norm = a => { const l = Math.hypot(a[0], a[1], a[2]) || 1; return [a[0] / l, a[1] / l, a[2] / l]; };\n1978\tSN.frame = (F, up = [0, 0, 1], bank = 0) => {          // -> { F, R, U }; bank > 0 lowers the right edge\n1979\t  const R0 = norm(cross(up, F)), U0 = cross(F, R0), c = Math.cos(bank), s = Math.sin(bank);\n1980\t  return { F, R: [R0[0] * c - U0[0] * s, R0[1] * c - U0[1] * s, R0[2] * c - U0[2] * s],\n1981\t              U: [U0[0] * c + R0[0] * s, U0[1] * c + R0[1] * s, U0[2] * c + R0[2] * s] };\n1982\t};\n1983\t// test: SN.frame([1,0,0]).R ≈ [0,1,0] (south = right when heading east); SN.frame([1,0,0],[0,0,1],.3).R[2] < 0 (right edge lower)\n1984\t```\n1985\t\n1986\t**World3D camera pose from a frame:**\n1987\t- `yaw = atan2(dir.y, dir.x)` and `pitch = asin(dir.z)` (negative looks down), where `dir` = unit(look − eye);\n1988\t- `roll = rollSign · atan2(dot(Ucam, Rflat), dot(Ucam, Zup))`, with `Rflat` = unit(cross(Zup, dir)) under the engine\n1989\t  convention.\n1990\t\n1991\tSet `rollSign` by the M3 screenshot check.\n1992\t\n1993\t## Appendix B: gibberish voice (`SN.Voice`)\n1994\t\n1995\t```js\n1996\t// say(text, v = { f0, speed, ring, crush, vol }) -> seconds; headless: computes the length, makes no sound\n1997\tfunction say(text, v) {\n1998\t  const words = text.toUpperCase().replace(/[^A-Z0-9?!.' ]/g, ' ').split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean);\n1999\t  let t = 0; const ctx = game.audio.ctx, out = sfxBus();            // the engine's effects bus: volume settings apply\n2000\t  for (const w of words) {\n2001\t    const rnd = E.rng(hashString(w)), n = Math.max(1, Math.round(w.replace(/[^A-Z]/g, '').length / 2.6));\n2002\t    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n2003\t      const ch = w[(i * 2 + 1) % w.length], vi = 'AEIOU'.indexOf(ch), vowel = 'AEIOU'[vi >= 0 ? vi : (rnd() * 5) | 0];\n2004\t      const dur = (0.07 + rnd() * 0.04) / v.speed, last = i === n - 1;\n2005\t      const bend = last && /[.]$/.test(w) ? 0.88 : last && /[?]$/.test(w) ? 1.18 : last && /!$/.test(w) ? 1.10 : 1;\n2006\t      const f = v.f0 * (0.92 + rnd() * 0.16) * bend;\n2007\t      if (ctx) { consonant(ctx, out, t, 2000 + rnd() * 3000, 0.018); vowelTone(ctx, out, t + 0.012, dur, f, FORMANTS[vowel], v); }\n2008\t      t += dur + 0.012;\n2009\t    }\n2010\t    t += 0.06 / v.speed;                                            // a gap between words\n2011\t  }\n2012\t  return t;\n2013\t}\n2014\t// FORMANTS = { A: [800, 1200], E: [400, 2000], I: [300, 2300], O: [450, 800], U: [325, 700] }\n2015\t// vowelTone: saw osc at f (+ vibrato 6 Hz, 1.5 %) -> two bandpass filters (F1, F2; Q 6) summed -> gain env (8 ms attack,\n2016\t// 30 ms release) [-> ring mod (osc * 60 Hz) for ORACLE; -> WaveShaper step curve for KAI-ZERO]; plus 15 % noise.\n2017\t```\n2018\t\n2019\t## Appendix C: planning-script results (`tools/trackcheck.mjs` must reproduce them)\n2020\t\n2021\tSpline: App. A, k = 48–96, resampled at 2 m (0.5 m for the jumps). Air gravity 40 m/s². Flights start from the lip\n2022\twith the lip's slope, 0.9 m above the surface.\n2023\t\n2024\t| Track | Length | Tightest radius | Slopes (outside jumps) | Overpass | Jump |\n2025\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n2026\t| Port Solenne | 3.84 km | 56 m (s ≈ 3412, lighthouse) | −5 … +5 % | none | drop cp12→14: an 8.6 m step, 0.65 s air at all speeds; impact 45 m/s −30°, 90 m/s −16°, 170 m/s −6° |\n2027\t| Karakum Spire | 4.59 km | 55 m (s ≈ 2408, the spiral) | −8 … +7 % | s 2208 under s 2928: 24.5 m | gap cp7→9, 57 m: 45 m/s hits the wall 20.6 m low, 60 m/s 6.6 m low, **75 m/s clears** (0 m past, −9°), 90 m/s +18 m (−13°), 115 +49 m, 140 +82 m, 170 +129 m (−10°) |\n2028\t| Meridian Stack | 4.18 km | 52 m (s ≈ 4167, before the start straight) | −4 … +4 % | s 2082 under s 3983: 31.9 m | drop cp4→6: a 14.2 m step; 45 m/s lands at −37° (hard), 90 m/s −21°, 140 m/s −12°, 170 m/s −11° |\n2029\t| Borealis Vault | 5.03 km | 44 m (s ≈ 3774, switchbacks) | −6 … +11 % | none | drop cp6→8: a 17.2 m step; 45 m/s −40° (hard), 90 m/s −23°, 115 m/s −15°, 170 m/s −12° (1.2 s air) |\n2030\t\n2031\tLap-time estimates are in §4.2. Hard landings (> 25°) cost energy and speed by design (§3.2 step 5). Slow craft\n2032\tare punished, fast ones reward.\n2033\t\n2034\t## Appendix D: AI Hub session skeleton (`90-hub.js`)\n2035\t\n2036\t```js\n2037\tSN.hub = { active: !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active), info: null, ghosts: new Map(), lastSend: 0, ended: false, reported: false };\n2038\tasync function startSession() {                               // called from the boot's last step when SN.hub.active\n2039\t  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n2040\t  if (!info) { SN.hub.active = false; return game.go('title'); }\n2041\t  SN.hub.info = info;\n2042\t  const ev = SN.hub.event = { track: ['solenne', 'karakum', 'meridian', 'borealis'][Math.floor(AIHub.rng('event')() * 4)],\n2043\t                              cls: 'FLARE', laps: 3, seed: Math.floor(AIHub.rng('race')() * 2 ** 32) };\n2044\t  for (const p of info.players) if (p.id !== info.me) SN.hub.ghosts.set(p.id, { id: p.id, name: p.name, color: p.color, s: [] });\n2045\t  AIHub.on('card', c => SN.hub.card = c);\n2046\t  AIHub.on('start', () => SN.hub.started = true);\n2047\t  AIHub.on('message', (d, from) => { const g = SN.hub.ghosts.get(from); if (g && d.t === 'g') g.s.push(Object.assign({ at: AIHub.time() }, d)); if (g && d.t === 'done') g.done = d.ms; });\n2048\t  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => SN.hub.ghosts.delete(id));\n2049\t  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (!SN.hub.reported) { SN.hub.reported = true; AIHub.result({ score: Math.round(myShip().p / 16) }); } });\n2050\t  AIHub.on('end', e => { SN.hub.ended = true; SN.hub.endInfo = e; SN.audio.stopAll(); });\n2051\t  game.go('loading', { next: 'session', track: ev.track, then: () => AIHub.ready() });   // ready() once the world is warm\n2052\t}\n2053\t// in the session scene's update: card UI until started; countdown from AIHub.time(); race.step only when time() >= 0 and !ended;\n2054\t// every 100 ms: AIHub.send({ t: 'g', p, u, h, y, r, v, lap, fin }, { reliable: false }); every 1000 ms: AIHub.progress({ score, label });\n2055\t// on finish: AIHub.result({ time: Math.round(AIHub.time()), stats, awards }); AIHub.send({ t: 'done', ms }); SN.hub.reported = true\n2056\t```\n2057\t\n2058\t## Appendix E: World3D facts learned in planning (saves the builders an afternoon)\n2059\t\n2060\t- The 3D add-on is an ES module that imports `three/webgpu`, `three/tsl` and `@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat` by bare\n2061\t  specifier. It needs an import map. It attaches `E.World3D`, `E.THREE`, `E.TSL` and `E.RAPIER`, and throws if the 2D\n2062\t  engine isn't loaded first.\n2063\t- `await E.World3D.init(game)` creates one renderer for the page: WebGPU, else WebGL 2 (`?backend=webgl` forces it).\n2064\t  It makes `#view` under `#screen` if missing. The game must use `bg: null`. It always initialises Rapier (so Rapier\n2065\t  must be loadable even though craft don't use it). Headless it returns at once.\n2066\t- `new E.World3D(game, { terrain | level, sky, fog, ambient, sun, lights, glowLights, shadows, filter, camera,\n2067\t  onDraw, overlay })`.\n2068\t  - `terrain` coordinates run from 0 to `size` (a power-of-two chunk count): keep tracks inside (hence `origin`).\n2069\t  - `world.scene` takes your own three.js meshes. Use **node materials only**: MeshLambert / MeshToon / MeshBasic\n2070\t    NodeMaterial. Never ShaderMaterial, WebGLRenderer or addons.\n2071\t  - Make the materials at world creation. `world.prepare()` builds the shaders. `world.dispose()` before making the\n2072\t    next world.\n2073\t- The camera has modes `view`, `chase`, `first`, `fly`, `fixed`, `zones` and `behind`. We use `fixed` with\n2074\t  `camera.fixed = { x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, fov }`. `camera.far` and `camera.near` are in units.\n2075\t  `world.addCamera(o)` plus `game.splitScreen(2)` makes a split screen (filters are off while split).\n2076\t  `world.project(x, y, z)` gives HUD pixels.\n2077\t- `world.step(dt)` in update and `world.draw(r)` in draw, then the HUD with `r.overlay`.\n2078\t- `game.particles.*` draw in 3D and land on `particles.ground`. World3D resets that every draw: see edit §2.7.5.\n2079\t- Its settings keys: `look3d`, `picture3d` (`pixels` | `balanced` | `full`), `shadows3d`, `filter3d` (`clean` |\n2080\t  `cel` | `pixel`). `filter.bloom` is a boolean in the world's `filter`.\n2081\t- Its own racing (`world.track`, `world.vehicle`, a Rapier ball) is **not** used. The craft need track-space physics\n2082\t  at Wipeout speeds (§3.2), and the tracks need tunnels, drops, gaps and overpasses that `world.track` doesn't model.\n2083\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4eed361-ef26-4b83-9819-20dffd5cdae7","uuid":"70563756-39b5-43f0-b86a-b0a160c71de4","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:47:07.653Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-184648__xa320fb/work/PLAN.md","content":"| 8 | SIDE-SHIFT | cp15 − 200 m | \"Mines ahead. Side-shift with {shiftL} or {shiftR} to slip past.\" | a mine line at cp15 + 40 m (3 mines spanning 2/3 of the width, the gap on the side away from the racing line) passed with no hit and a side-shift used in the last 1.5 s |\n| 9 | BARREL ROLL | cp11 − 100 m (about 2.5 s before the lip), at 300 km/h | \"Off the Harbour Step, flick {steer} left-right, or press {shiftL}/{shiftR} in the air. Land the roll for a boost.\" | a `roll` event with `ok` |\n| 10 | PIT LANE | cp21 + 0 m, energy 40 % | \"Shield low. Ride the green pit strip to recharge to full.\" | energy ≥ 99 |\n| 11 | FULL LAP | grid, standing start | \"Put it together. One lap under sixty seconds.\" | a lap ≤ 60.0 s at SPARK (the ideal line is about 46 s) |\n\n\n**Race radio:** a pool of about 30 short lines, gibberish plus subtitle in the radio box, rate-limited to one per\n12 s. Triggers: overtaking or being overtaken by a named pilot, a weapon hit, an elimination, the final lap. Speakers\nare the pilots (§4.1 banter, plus 2 more each), for example:\n- \"Make room.\" / \"Too slow, rookie.\" / \"That one stung.\" / \"Shield's holding.\" / \"Pit lane, now.\" (own team)\n- RIVAL: \"Behind you. Still.\" / \"Smile for the wreck report.\"\n\n### 4.6 Sponsors and signage (`66-scenery.js` canvas textures)\n\nFictional brands for gantries, billboards, wall panels and holograms. Each is a logo (a geometric mark drawn in px)\nplus a name and a slogan, in the engine's pixel font at scale 2–4 on 128–256 px canvases:\n\n| Brand | Slogan |\n| --- | --- |\n| QWIK-FUEL | FILL UP. FALL UP. |\n| OKTA NOODLE | EAT AT 600 KM/H |\n| HALCYON BANK | YOUR MONEY, FASTER |\n| AXON AIR | BREATHE PREMIUM |\n| VANTA PAINTS | DARKER THAN NOTHING |\n| MERIDIAN TELECOM | ALWAYS ON. ALWAYS. |\n| POLARIS COLD STORAGE | WE KEEP IT FROM YOU |\n| NOVA-CHROME | SHINE RESPONSIBLY |\n| KIBO TEA | STEEPED IN THE FUTURE |\n| ORBIT SOCKS | KEEP YOUR FEET IN ORBIT |\n| THE AUTHORITY | DO NOT LOOK DIRECTLY AT THE FUTURE |\n| SOLENNE TOURISM | COME FOR THE SEA. STAY FOR THE SPEED. |\n\nSignage: SECTOR markers 1–8, PIT, the jump warnings (\"GORGE: 270 KM/H MINIMUM\"), and chevron boards.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Build order and milestones\n\nThe ordering principle: **the riskiest unknown first**. First the 3D stack in one file, then the core loop (one craft\non one track), then a full race (AI and weapons). Breadth comes after that (modes, UI, season, audio), then\nintegration (attract, dev, hub). Polish is last. Each milestone ends with its tests passing in `node tests/run.mjs`.\n\n| # | Milestone | Deliverables | Exit tests (all automated unless marked 📷 = screenshot review) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **M0** | Skeleton and stack spike | Dev folder, pinned downloads (§2.1), `package.json`, `tests/run.mjs` and `tests/lib/vm.mjs`, `tools/bundle.mjs`, `index.html`. A minimal `95-main.js`: `new E.Game` with SN.INPUT, the boot steps (the 3D wait/init), a test oval TrackDef rendered as a plain ribbon mesh in a terrain world, a dummy craft box moving along it at 2000 u/s, the chase cam, an overlay text | Node: the game boots headless and `advance(5)` runs with no errors. Browser: the bundle opens from file:// with no page errors; `World3D.backend` is 'WebGPU' or 'WebGL 2'; the #view canvas is non-black over > 30 % of its area; it reaches race view in < 15 s. 📷 the ribbon and box |\n| **M1** | Tracks | `20-track.js` complete: spline, slices, frames, bank, features, surface, locate, query, line, speed profile, validation, minimap. `07-data-tracks.js` with all 4 tracks. `tools/trackcheck.mjs` | unit: frame handedness (8 headings), bank sign, closure continuity (`C(L−ε) ≈ C(0)`), arc-length error < 0.1 %, lengths within 1 % of §4.3, overpass clearances (24.5 / 31.9 m ±0.5), the `{cp,d}` feature s-values, the racing line inside the bounds, speed profile ≤ top. 📷 an overhead debug render of each track with features |\n| **M2** | One craft that flies right | `25-ship.js`, `27-collide.js` (bodies only), `01-input.js` (mapping, double tap, flick, vpad), Tune registry, engine edits §2.7.1–3 (glyphs default, font glyphs, analog values) and §2.7.5. A player craft on any track, keyboard and pad | physics suite (§7.2): the feel targets of §3.2, walls never crossed at 3000 u/s, no NaN in 10 min of random input, the jumps per App. C at each class, drop landings, overpass stability (s never jumps levels), pads, pit, side-shift lateral 3–5 m, the barrel-roll boost and botch, rescue after a fall, a simple line bot (`T.line` + `T.vline` with PD steering) laps every track × class with 0 rescues |\n| **M3** | It looks like the game | `60-render.js` (worlds, interpolation, cameras), `64-trackmesh.js` (surface, walls with neon and chevrons, pads, tunnels, supports, gantries, drop and gap faces), `62-shipkit.js` (6 craft, liveries, flaps, glow, trails, roll), the themes' sky/fog/sun and terrain carve, basic scenery per theme, bloom | browser: each track loads in < 10 s; no shader stalls over 50 ms after GO (frame-time log); 📷 per track: the start grid, a banked corner (roll sign), a tunnel, the jump, the overpass from both decks; all 6 craft on the turntable |\n| **M4** | A real race | `40-race.js` (lifecycle, grid, countdown and launch revs, laps, sectors, positions, wrong way, finish, results, elimination), `35-ai.js` (line, speed, control, avoidance, pads, mistakes, rubber band, difficulty), `45-replay.js` (record and replay, hash) | race suite: an 8-AI race on every track × class finishes; no craft stuck > 3 s; ≤ 1 rescue per craft per race; lap times within ±25 % of §4.2; positions consistent with progress; `hash` equal on two runs from the same seed; a replay re-sim gives an equal hash; wrong-way detection; the launch-boost window |\n| **M5** | Combat | `30-weapons.js` (pads, roll table, 10 weapons, absorb, lock-on, damage, stagger), AI weapon logic, `68-fx.js` for every weapon, events wired to interim SFX (`audio.define` voices; M9 replaces every one, and none may remain) | weapons suite: each weapon fired by a scripted craft at a target in a fixed setup deals its damage; the target's warning appears; BULWARK blocks; absorb adds energy; MINEFIELD triggers; TREMOR misses airborne craft; SIPHON transfers; RAILSHOT hits within its aim tolerance and misses outside; elimination at 0 (DNF in a race, respawn in SNIPEOUT); in an 8-AI race every weapon is used at least once across 4 seeded races |\n| **M6** | HUD and front-end | `70-hud.js`, `55-glyphs.js`, `75-ui.js` (widget kit, every §3.9 screen), settings (§3.17), pause items, the touch-only notice, the About skeleton | flow suite: title → menu → quick race setup → loading → race → results → menu by scripted taps; mouse hover focus (`input.feed('move')`) and click activation; the prompt bar switches device (key, pad stub, mouse); Button symbols switches PS ↔ Xbox labels; the touch-only notice when `matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)')` is false and `maxTouchPoints > 0` (stubbed in vm), with no touch buttons (`input.touchButtons` never called). 📷 every screen at 1280×720 and 1920×1080 |\n| **M7** | Every mode | TIME TRIAL plus ghosts, HOT LAP, SNIPEOUT, OVERCLOCK plus the skin, ACADEMY (11 drills, drone, gates, mine line), VERSUS (join, half keys, split HUD), the REPLAY scene, records | modes suite: each mode starts, plays, and ends with correct results; ghost save/load round-trips and plays back aligned (< 1 m error); Overclock zones advance and the run ends at 0 energy; the academy bot passes all drills; versus with 2 inputs makes 2 viewports and both finish; replay click-to-follow selects the clicked craft (feed a click at a projected position) |\n| **M8** | Season and story | `08-data-season.js`, `09-data-story.js`, `78-season-ui.js` (hub, briefings, GP, ending, credits), saves, unlocks | season suite: the **scripted playthrough** (§7.4) of the whole season with the player bot; unlocks fire in order; save → reload → state equal; every dialog line references only defined vars; every event playable |\n| **M9** | Sound | engine edit §2.7.4; `50-audio.js`: 6 songs and stings, the full SFX catalogue, engine hums, the music director (layers, final lap, overclock tempo), `SN.Voice` gibberish, announcer callouts, radio | audio suite (headless, no WebAudio): every song parses with no engine warnings and is ≥ 16 bars; each event type maps to an existing sound; `Voice.say` durations are > 0 and stable per word; the music layers react to race events (`audio.pos.layers`). 🔊 a human-free check: in the browser, record `audio.drift` stays < 10 ms and no audio errors |\n| **M10** | Attract and dev | `85-attract.js`, `80-dev.js` (panel, cheats, sliders, reset, overlays, info) | flow: 10.0 s idle on the title → attract starts (not at 9.9 s); any of key/pad/click exits within 1 step; the attract shows ≥ 8 distinct weapons and ≥ 3 tracks across one loop (counted from events); dev: every slider changes `SN.Tune.T` and the sim responds (e.g., topSpeedMul 1.5 raises top speed); RESET ALL restores every default exactly; each cheat works |\n| **M11** | AI Hub | `90-hub.js`, its own card, ghost send/receive, the session scene | hub suite (Node mock of `AIHub`, §7.6) and the **real harness** (§7.6): `players=2&auto=1`, `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, `…&scenario=host-leave`; `__hubCheck.pass === true` in each |\n| **M12** | Polish and ship | scenery density, effects, juice (shake, flashes, rumble via `input.rumble`), the balance pass with the sliders, medal calibration (`tools/medals.mjs`), the About pages filled, `exit-interview.json`, the final bundle | the full `node tests/run.mjs` passes; `tools/bundle.mjs` passes its checks (no TODO, an identical hub client); `node engine/handoff/tools/check.mjs ../<bundle>.html` gives no errors (it will list the CDN files as external, which is expected); 📷 the final screenshot set (§7.7) |\n\n**The vertical slice at the end of M5** must already *play* like the game: a full race with AI and weapons on every\ntrack. If time runs short later, the plan's priorities hold:\n1. a feature's existence and correctness (§8);\n2. the playthrough test;\n3. the look;\n4. the quantity of content.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Risks and how to de-risk them\n\n| # | Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk (when) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | **The 3D stack in one file** (an inline ES module, an import map to the CDN, file://, WebGPU → WebGL 2 fallback, headless Chromium) | Nothing else works if it doesn't. It is new to most builders | **M0 spike first.** Prove the bundle from file:// in Playwright with a picture. If the CDN is blocked in the test environment, retry once, then vendor `three.webgpu.min.js`, `three.core.min.js` (imported by it), `three.tsl.min.js` and `rapier.mjs` as inline modules: rewrite the import map to `data:`/blob URLs made by a tiny classic loader, or inline the files as `<script type=\"module\">` with the specifiers mapped to blob URLs. Keep the CDN as the default (smaller file) |\n| 2 | **Frame and handedness bugs** (a left-handed engine frame, bank signs, camera roll sign, `toThree`) | Silent wrongness: mirrored steering, banks the wrong way, a camera rolling backwards | Unit tests in M1 (§7.2) before any physics. One `SN.frame` helper, used everywhere. A screenshot check of the roll on the Karakum spiral (M3) |\n| 3 | **Physics at 3,000 u/s** (tunnelling, jitter on crests, stuck on walls, overpasses confusing the track lookup) | The core feel. Hard to see in code review | Track-space walls are analytic (no tunnelling). Local-only `locate`. Invariant tests over long random-input runs (M2). Dev sliders for live tuning. The App. C jump numbers become tests |\n| 4 | **AI that finishes on every track** (the jump speeds, hairpins, overpass, open edges, the drop in a curve) | A stuck AI breaks races, attract, the season playthrough and medal calibration | One line/profile generator plus a PD controller, tested on 4 tracks × 4 classes × 4 seeds in M4. A stuck detector, rescue, and a per-track min-speed constraint at the gap |\n| 5 | **Determinism** (replays, the hub's fair start, hashes) | Any `Math.random`, dt or order dependence breaks replays | §2.8 rules. A lint test that greps the sim files for `Math.random`, `Date.now` and `performance.now`. Hash-equality tests from M4 on |\n| 6 | **Shader stalls and loading hitches** (World3D compiles on first use) | Visible hitches at GO or on the first weapon | Materials only at world creation. The warm-up frame and `world.prepare()` in loading (§3.7). Frame-time logging in the M3 browser test |\n| 7 | **Scope** (11 modes, 4 tracks, season, audio, hub) | Running out of time with stubs left (the brief forbids stubs) | Milestone order puts every feature in a minimal complete form before polish. The §8 checklist is the definition of done. Cut quantity, never features |\n| 8 | **Hub conformance** (card, ready without keys, time-up, end, ghosts) | The hub keeps failing games out of sessions | The Node mock early (M11 start), then the real harness at 1, 2 and 4 players with network faults and host-leave. The session path shares the race code, so it adds little new code |\n| 9 | **Synth music quality** | Bad music undermines the source's identity | The engine edits (filter env, unison) make house/acid/trance timbres possible. Compose at least 16 bars with A/B sections and use layers. A headless check that songs parse. A listen in the browser (the builder has no ears, so check with `audio.pos` and drift) |\n| 10 | **Readability at 10 feet** (a 427×240 HUD on a TV) | Tiny text is the default trap | HUD at scale 2 minimum for numbers, the large-HUD option, ≤ 6 items per screen. Screenshots at 1920×1080 scaled down to 50 % must stay legible (📷 M6) |\n| 11 | **Analog triggers and DualSense mapping** | The engine reads only `pressed` | Engine edit §2.7.3, tested with a stubbed `navigator.getGamepads()` in Playwright (axes and button `value`) |\n| 12 | **/tmp nearly full** (a shared tmpfs) | Playwright and Chromium need temp space | `TMPDIR=<dev>/.tmp` for every tool run (§0) |\n| 13 | **Terrain intersecting the track or tunnels** | The ground poking through decks or tunnel interiors looks broken | The corridor grid carve (§3.7) plus portal frames. 📷 every tunnel portal and every elevated section in M3 |\n\n---\n\n## 7. Testing (one command)\n\n**The command:** `cd SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174728 && TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp node tests/run.mjs`.\nIt runs every suite (Node first, then browser, then the hub harness). It prints **only failures** (suite › test:\nmessage, plus the snapshot JSON where useful) and **one final line**:\n`412 passed, 0 failed (node 380, browser 22, hub 10) in 96 s`.\n- `node tests/run.mjs physics race` runs only the named suites.\n- `--node` skips the browser and hub suites.\n- Rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers (the suites map to files, listed in `tests/run.mjs`).\n\n### 7.1 Harness\n\n`tests/lib/vm.mjs` follows the handoff's `game/test.mjs` and `kits/test.mjs`:\n- a `vm` context with stand-ins `window = ctx`, `addEventListener() {}`, `location: { search: '', hash: '' }`,\n  `matchMedia`, `navigator: { maxTouchPoints: 0, getGamepads: () => [] }`;\n- it runs `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, then the `src/` files in manifest order;\n- `E.current` is the game, and `game.advance(s)` drives it;\n- scripted input through `game.input.tap/hold/press`, `input.feed` for the mouse, and `SN.vpad` for analog;\n- assertions through `game.debug.snapshot()`.\n\n```js\ngame.debug = {\n  snapshot: () => ({ scene, state, mode, track, cls, t, ships: [{ id, p, s, u, h, v, kmh, energy, lap, place, weapon, airborne, finished, elim }],\n                     player: {...}, hudCallouts: [...], focus: ui.focusId, device: input.lastDevice, attract: bool, dev: bool,\n                     season: { medals, unlocked }, hub: { connected, sent, progressCount } }),\n  teleport(s, u = 0, v = 0), give(weapon), setEnergy(x), finishNow(), events: () => race.events.slice(),\n  race: () => race, track: () => track, tune: SN.Tune\n};\n```\n\n### 7.2 Node suites (fast, about 60 s in all)\n\n- **unit:**\n  - math and frames (8 headings), bank sign, `toThree` mapping;\n  - the spline: closure, arc length, knot s;\n  - each TrackDef validates;\n  - feature s-values; `query` returns the right deck at overpasses;\n  - the racing line inside the bounds; speed profile ≤ top;\n  - Tune def/reset;\n  - the input mapping: double-tap, flick, ramped keys;\n  - the hash is stable;\n  - **lint:** the sim files contain no `Math.random`, `Date.now`, `performance.now`, `alert(`, `confirm(`, `prompt(`\n    or `window.open`, and no file contains TODO.\n- **physics:**\n  - every feel target in §3.2;\n  - jumps: Karakum's gap at 70 / 80 / 90 / 140 m/s (fails at 70, clears at ≥ 80, landing window as App. C ±15 %), drops\n    land at 45 and 170 m/s;\n  - long random-input soak (10 simulated minutes, 4 tracks): no NaN, never `|u| > hw` on walled decks, never `h < 0`;\n  - overpass: a craft on the upper deck stays on it (its s stays in the upper range);\n  - pads, pit recharge, side-shift, roll ok/botch, rescue after an open-edge fall;\n  - launch boost window.\n- **race:**\n  - 4 tracks × 4 classes × 2 seeds of 8 AI: all finish, no stuck, rescues ≤ 1 per craft, lap times within ±25 % of\n    §4.2;\n  - positions sorted by progress; wrong way; final-lap event; results;\n  - determinism (2 runs, equal hash); replay re-sim equals the hash.\n- **weapons:** every row of §3.4, each in a fixed two-craft setup, plus AI usage counts.\n- **modes:** time trial (+ ghost round trip), hot lap (flying start, best lap), snipeout (scoring, respawn, the target\n  ends it), overclock (zones, tempo events, end), academy (the bot passes 11 drills), versus (2 viewports, half-keys\n  labels), grand prix (points table, ties).\n- **flow:**\n  - title → menu → setup → race → results → replay → menu;\n  - pause menu items present (Restart, Camera, How to play, Dev mode, Quit) and absent in a session;\n  - settings keys exist;\n  - glyph labels per device and setting;\n  - touch-only notice;\n  - attract timing and exit;\n  - dev sliders and reset; each cheat.\n- **season:** §7.4.\n- **audio:** song parsing, event → sound map, `Voice` durations, the music director's layer changes (headless:\n  `audio.pos`).\n- **hub (mock):** §7.6.\n\n### 7.3 The player bot (`tests/lib/bot.mjs`)\n\n`bot.drive(playerIndex, { skill: 1, weapons: true, rolls: true })`. Each step it computes `SN.AI.controls(ship, race)`\nfor the human's craft and writes them into `SN.vpad[i]`. Edge actions (fire, absorb, side-shift) go through\n`input.tap`, so the human path (mapping, double-tap, flick) is exercised. `bot.menu(path)` navigates screens by\nwidget id: it taps the arrows to reach the focus, then confirm.\n\n### 7.4 Scripted playthrough of the whole game (the season suite and the `playthrough` test)\n\nOne test plays the game end to end, headless, on fixed seeds, asserting along the way:\n1. Boot → title.\n2. Wait 10 s → attract (assert it is running, weapons seen, at least 2 tracks across the playlist with\n   `game.advance(120)`) → a key press → title.\n3. → menu → ACADEMY (the bot passes the drills) → SEASON: prologue → E1…E10 in order, each via the season hub, bot\n   driving, ≥ bronze (retry up to 3 times, asserting progress), the briefings advanced by taps.\n4. Promotions unlock FLARE and STORM.\n5. GP: 4 races; assert the points and the standings screen.\n6. The ending lines and the credits play; SINGULARITY is unlocked.\n7. Then QUICK RACE at SINGULARITY on Borealis; TIME TRIAL Karakum (a ghost saved, then loaded on the next run); HOT\n   LAP Meridian; SNIPEOUT Solenne; OVERCLOCK to zone 10; VERSUS with `game.addPlayer({ keys: 'right' })` and two\n   bots; REPLAY of the last race (hash equal).\n8. The pause menu → Dev mode → slider → reset → close; Settings → Button symbols → Xbox (labels change); About pages\n   1–5.\n9. `game.errors.length === 0` throughout.\n\n### 7.5 Browser suites (Playwright, Chromium headless; `tests/browser/`)\n\n- `bundle loads`: file:// URL; no `pageerror`; `My3D2dge.World3D.backend` is set; the boot completes in < 20 s.\n- `renders`: in the race, sample the `#view` canvas (`toDataURL` or a screenshot) and require at least 40 % non-black\n  pixels and > 24 distinct colours; the HUD canvas is drawn.\n- `input devices`:\n  - keyboard thrust raises the speed;\n  - stubbed `navigator.getGamepads()` (a DualSense-like id, standard mapping): ✕ thrust, L2 `value: .5` halves the\n    airbrake, and prompts show ✕/□/○ glyphs;\n  - the Xbox setting shows A/X/B;\n  - the mouse hovers and clicks a menu tile.\n- `screens`: the flow through the menus with screenshots to `tests/out/` (📷 reviewed by the builder only for look:\n  layout, legibility, art).\n- `split screen`: 2 viewports draw two different camera poses (the pixels differ between the halves).\n- `touch-only`: emulate a phone (`hasTouch`, coarse pointer, no keyboard events) → the notice and the SETTINGS button\n  are visible, and no engine touch buttons are drawn; after 10 s the attract runs.\n- **Performance is out of scope** (TASK.md), but log the median frame time per track to `tests/out/perf.json` for\n  information.\n\n### 7.6 AI Hub tests\n\n- **Node mock** (`tests/hub/mock.mjs`): a fake `AIHub` installed before the game's scripts (`active: true`, `connect`\n  resolves `info` for seat 1 of 2, events delivered by the test). It asserts:\n  - no title or menu scenes are entered;\n  - `ready()` is called exactly once with no input;\n  - nothing moves before `start`;\n  - the race begins at `time() ≥ 0`;\n  - `progress` is called ≥ once a second, with a numeric score and a label;\n  - `send` is ≤ 20/s, unreliable, ≤ 16 KB;\n  - an incoming message creates and moves a ghost;\n  - `leave` removes it;\n  - `result({ time })` on finish (bot);\n  - `time-up` before the finish → `result({ score })` once;\n  - `end` → input ignored, music stopped, no further `send`;\n  - `card` events: Enter → `answer('ready')`, △ → `answer('more')`.\n- **Real harness** (`tests/hub/hub.test.mjs`):\n  1. Copy the bundle into a scratch dir inside `tests/out/hub/` with the pinned `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and\n     `round.js`.\n  2. Spawn `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` there (`-u`: unbuffered, so the \"Serving HTTP on 127.0.0.1\n     port N\" line arrives at once), and parse the port from it.\n  3. Fetch `/<bundle>.html` and confirm its `<title>` is `Snipeout HD` (it is our page).\n  4. Open `harness.html?game=<bundle>.html&players=2&auto=1` in Playwright, wait for `body[data-complete=\"true\"]`\n     (timeout 240 s), and read `window.__hubCheck`. Require `pass === true`, and print the failed checks otherwise.\n  5. Repeat with `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, and with `&scenario=host-leave`.\n  6. Kill the server **by its PID** (the child process you spawned).\n\n### 7.7 Screenshots (only for what scripts can't judge)\n\nPer track:\n- grid at the countdown;\n- chase cam mid-corner (bank and roll);\n- cockpit;\n- tunnel;\n- jump in flight;\n- overpass from below and above (Karakum, Meridian);\n- a weapon effect (each weapon once across tracks);\n- the Overclock skin at zone 1 and zone 20;\n- split screen.\n\nScreens: title, attract with DEMO, every menu screen, team select (each craft), results with podium, the season hub,\na briefing with portrait, the dev panel (each tab), About pages, the touch-only notice, the hub card.\n\nReview them for: legibility at 10 feet (view at 50 %), contrast, colour-only information, a HUD clear of the corner,\nnothing clipped at 4:3, 16:9 or 21:9 (`expand: true` sizes: 1024×768, 1280×720, 2560×1080).\n\n---\n\n## 8. Definition of done: every TASK.md requirement, where it lives, how it is proven\n\n| TASK.md requirement | Where in the game | Proof |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Genre and perspective that fit the source | anti-gravity combat racing; chase, far and cockpit cams plus TV cameras (§1, §3.6) | 📷 M3 |\n| Title: a riff picked by a real RNG | **Snipeout HD** (§0, `secrets.randbelow`) | — |\n| One HTML file named `SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174728.html` (CDN dependencies allowed) | `tools/bundle.mjs` (§2.3) | browser: bundle loads |\n| Dev files in the subfolder; bundle in the root | §2.2 | — |\n| Built on the handoff; engine changes allowed | §2.1, §2.7 (marked edits) | About → engine changes |\n| Art: the engine's native style plus new assets that feel like the source | pixel-res World3D, toon/lambert, pixel HUD/fonts; new craft, tracks, neon, sponsors (§3.7, §4) | 📷 |\n| Animation: the engine's system plus new animations | rigs (cards, poses `cheer` / `wave` / `hips`, portraits that talk), tweens/scripts; new procedural craft animation (roll, flaps, glow, trails, barrel roll, explosions, drone), HUD/menu tweens (§3.7, §3.8) | 📷 |\n| Audio all in code; gibberish voices | the synth plus edits, 6 songs, SFX, hums, `SN.Voice` (§3.10) | audio suite |\n| Online: AI Hub integration, and multiplayer for the game on its own | ghost-mode sessions (§3.16); local 2P split-screen VERSUS | hub mock + real harness; versus test |\n| Feature-complete demo, long enough to show every mechanic | 11 modes, the season with a GP and an ending, the academy (§1, §3.3, §4.5) | the playthrough §7.4 |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu; live sliders and reset | §3.15 | flow: dev |\n| Attract mode: 10 s idle, AI demo, any input exits, may cheat | §3.14 | flow: attract |\n| Narrative tone like the source | §3.11, §4.5 | review |\n| 10-foot, controller-first, DualSense standard mapping | §3.9; analog triggers (§2.7.3) | browser: input devices |\n| Keyboard native, PC keys; mouse aims, looks, clicks; hover moves focus | §1 controls; mouse menus, fire/absorb, click-to-follow in replays, drag-rotate in team select | flow + browser |\n| Prompts follow the last device; PlayStation default; Settings option for Xbox | `55-glyphs.js`; `glyphs` default and option in Settings (§2.7.1) | flow + browser |\n| No dense web-style data screens | ≤ 6 items, big type, one row per craft (§3.9) | 📷 |\n| Touch-only: no touch controls, \"Controller or keyboard required\" plus a settings button, attract runs | §3.9 / §3.14 | browser: touch-only |\n| No TODOs, placeholders, stubs | bundle lint, unit lint (§2.3, §7.2) | tests |\n| Testing: headless scripts, `game.advance` / `game.debug`, a scripted whole-game playthrough, one command, failures only plus a one-line count | §7 | `node tests/run.mjs` |\n| Servers on 127.0.0.1 port 0, our page confirmed, stopped by PID | §7.6 | hub test |\n| Source Information, Testing/Engine/Prompt Feedback in the chat reply **and** the About/Credits screen | §3.18 | About pages; reply |\n| `exit-interview.json` in the exact shape, parses | `tools/exit-interview.mjs` (§3.18) | the script checks `JSON.parse` |\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A: reference code (use as is)\n\n**Centripetal Catmull-Rom (closed) and the arc-length resample.** This is the code the planning checker used. The §4.3\nnumbers come from it.\n\n```js\n// P: [[x, y, z], ...] closed loop; returns dense samples [[x, y, z, segIndex], ...] (k per segment)\nfunction catmullClosed(P, k = 64) {\n  const n = P.length, out = [], d = (a, b) => Math.hypot(b[0] - a[0], b[1] - a[1], b[2] - a[2]);\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n    const p0 = P[(i - 1 + n) % n], p1 = P[i], p2 = P[(i + 1) % n], p3 = P[(i + 2) % n];\n    const t0 = 0, t1 = Math.sqrt(d(p0, p1)), t2 = t1 + Math.sqrt(d(p1, p2)), t3 = t2 + Math.sqrt(d(p2, p3));   // alpha 0.5\n    for (let j = 0; j < k; j++) {\n      const t = t1 + (t2 - t1) * j / k, q = [];\n      for (let c = 0; c < 3; c++) {\n        const A1 = (t1 - t) / (t1 - t0) * p0[c] + (t - t0) / (t1 - t0) * p1[c];\n        const A2 = (t2 - t) / (t2 - t1) * p1[c] + (t - t1) / (t2 - t1) * p2[c];\n        const A3 = (t3 - t) / (t3 - t2) * p2[c] + (t - t2) / (t3 - t2) * p3[c];\n        const B1 = (t2 - t) / (t2 - t0) * A1 + (t - t0) / (t2 - t0) * A2;\n        const B2 = (t3 - t) / (t3 - t1) * A2 + (t - t1) / (t3 - t1) * A3;\n        q.push((t2 - t) / (t2 - t1) * B1 + (t - t1) / (t2 - t1) * B2);\n      }\n      out.push([q[0], q[1], q[2], i]);                 // (j === 0: exactly control point i: its knot)\n    }\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n// resample at a fixed spacing ds; returns { L, ds, pts, knots } (knots[i] = s of control point i)\nfunction resampleClosed(dense, ds) {\n  const n = dense.length, acc = [0], knots = [];\n  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) { const a = dense[i - 1], b = dense[i % n]; acc.push(acc[i - 1] + Math.hypot(b[0] - a[0], b[1] - a[1], b[2] - a[2])); }\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) if (i === 0 || dense[i][3] !== dense[i - 1][3]) knots[dense[i][3]] = acc[i];\n  const L = acc[n], m = Math.round(L / ds), step = L / m, pts = [];\n  for (let k = 0, j = 0; k < m; k++) {\n    const s = k * step; while (acc[j + 1] < s) j++;\n    const a = dense[j], b = dense[(j + 1) % n], f = (s - acc[j]) / (acc[j + 1] - acc[j]);\n    pts.push([a[0] + (b[0] - a[0]) * f, a[1] + (b[1] - a[1]) * f, a[2] + (b[2] - a[2]) * f]);\n  }\n  return { L, ds: step, pts, knots };\n}\n```\n\n**Frame helper (engine axes, left-handed: right = cross(up, forward)):**\n\n```js\nconst cross = (a, b) => [a[1] * b[2] - a[2] * b[1], a[2] * b[0] - a[0] * b[2], a[0] * b[1] - a[1] * b[0]];\nconst norm = a => { const l = Math.hypot(a[0], a[1], a[2]) || 1; return [a[0] / l, a[1] / l, a[2] / l]; };\nSN.frame = (F, up = [0, 0, 1], bank = 0) => {          // -> { F, R, U }; bank > 0 lowers the right edge\n  const R0 = norm(cross(up, F)), U0 = cross(F, R0), c = Math.cos(bank), s = Math.sin(bank);\n  return { F, R: [R0[0] * c - U0[0] * s, R0[1] * c - U0[1] * s, R0[2] * c - U0[2] * s],\n              U: [U0[0] * c + R0[0] * s, U0[1] * c + R0[1] * s, U0[2] * c + R0[2] * s] };\n};\n// test: SN.frame([1,0,0]).R ≈ [0,1,0] (south = right when heading east); SN.frame([1,0,0],[0,0,1],.3).R[2] < 0 (right edge lower)\n```\n\n**World3D camera pose from a frame:**\n- `yaw = atan2(dir.y, dir.x)` and `pitch = asin(dir.z)` (negative looks down), where `dir` = unit(look − eye);\n- `roll = rollSign · atan2(dot(Ucam, Rflat), dot(Ucam, Zup))`, with `Rflat` = unit(cross(Zup, dir)) under the engine\n  convention.\n\nSet `rollSign` by the M3 screenshot check.\n\n## Appendix B: gibberish voice (`SN.Voice`)\n\n```js\n// say(text, v = { f0, speed, ring, crush, vol }) -> seconds; headless: computes the length, makes no sound\nfunction say(text, v) {\n  const words = text.toUpperCase().replace(/[^A-Z0-9?!.' ]/g, ' ').split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean);\n  let t = 0; const ctx = game.audio.ctx, out = sfxBus();            // the engine's effects bus: volume settings apply\n  for (const w of words) {\n    const rnd = E.rng(hashString(w)), n = Math.max(1, Math.round(w.replace(/[^A-Z]/g, '').length / 2.6));\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n      const ch = w[(i * 2 + 1) % w.length], vi = 'AEIOU'.indexOf(ch), vowel = 'AEIOU'[vi >= 0 ? vi : (rnd() * 5) | 0];\n      const dur = (0.07 + rnd() * 0.04) / v.speed, last = i === n - 1;\n      const bend = last && /[.]$/.test(w) ? 0.88 : last && /[?]$/.test(w) ? 1.18 : last && /!$/.test(w) ? 1.10 : 1;\n      const f = v.f0 * (0.92 + rnd() * 0.16) * bend;\n      if (ctx) { consonant(ctx, out, t, 2000 + rnd() * 3000, 0.018); vowelTone(ctx, out, t + 0.012, dur, f, FORMANTS[vowel], v); }\n      t += dur + 0.012;\n    }\n    t += 0.06 / v.speed;                                            // a gap between words\n  }\n  return t;\n}\n// FORMANTS = { A: [800, 1200], E: [400, 2000], I: [300, 2300], O: [450, 800], U: [325, 700] }\n// vowelTone: saw osc at f (+ vibrato 6 Hz, 1.5 %) -> two bandpass filters (F1, F2; Q 6) summed -> gain env (8 ms attack,\n// 30 ms release) [-> ring mod (osc * 60 Hz) for ORACLE; -> WaveShaper step curve for KAI-ZERO]; plus 15 % noise.\n```\n\n## Appendix C: planning-script results (`tools/trackcheck.mjs` must reproduce them)\n\nSpline: App. A, k = 48–96, resampled at 2 m (0.5 m for the jumps). Air gravity 40 m/s². Flights start from the lip\nwith the lip's slope, 0.9 m above the surface.\n\n| Track | Length | Tightest radius | Slopes (outside jumps) | Overpass | Jump |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Port Solenne | 3.84 km | 56 m (s ≈ 3412, lighthouse) | −5 … +5 % | none | drop cp12→14: an 8.6 m step, 0.65 s air at all speeds; impact 45 m/s −30°, 90 m/s −16°, 170 m/s −6° |\n| Karakum Spire | 4.59 km | 55 m (s ≈ 2408, the spiral) | −8 … +7 % | s 2208 under s 2928: 24.5 m | gap cp7→9, 57 m: 45 m/s hits the wall 20.6 m low, 60 m/s 6.6 m low, **75 m/s clears** (0 m past, −9°), 90 m/s +18 m (−13°), 115 +49 m, 140 +82 m, 170 +129 m (−10°) |\n| Meridian Stack | 4.18 km | 52 m (s ≈ 4167, before the start straight) | −4 … +4 % | s 2082 under s 3983: 31.9 m | drop cp4→6: a 14.2 m step; 45 m/s lands at −37° (hard), 90 m/s −21°, 140 m/s −12°, 170 m/s −11° |\n| Borealis Vault | 5.03 km | 44 m (s ≈ 3774, switchbacks) | −6 … +11 % | none | drop cp6→8: a 17.2 m step; 45 m/s −40° (hard), 90 m/s −23°, 115 m/s −15°, 170 m/s −12° (1.2 s air) |\n\nLap-time estimates are in §4.2. Hard landings (> 25°) cost energy and speed by design (§3.2 step 5). Slow craft\nare punished, fast ones reward.\n\n## Appendix D: AI Hub session skeleton (`90-hub.js`)\n\n```js\nSN.hub = { active: !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active), info: null, ghosts: new Map(), lastSend: 0, ended: false, reported: false };\nasync function startSession() {                               // called from the boot's last step when SN.hub.active\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n  if (!info) { SN.hub.active = false; return game.go('title'); }\n  SN.hub.info = info;\n  const ev = SN.hub.event = { track: ['solenne', 'karakum', 'meridian', 'borealis'][Math.floor(AIHub.rng('event')() * 4)],\n                              cls: 'FLARE', laps: 3, seed: Math.floor(AIHub.rng('race')() * 2 ** 32) };\n  for (const p of info.players) if (p.id !== info.me) SN.hub.ghosts.set(p.id, { id: p.id, name: p.name, color: p.color, s: [] });\n  AIHub.on('card', c => SN.hub.card = c);\n  AIHub.on('start', () => SN.hub.started = true);\n  AIHub.on('message', (d, from) => { const g = SN.hub.ghosts.get(from); if (g && d.t === 'g') g.s.push(Object.assign({ at: AIHub.time() }, d)); if (g && d.t === 'done') g.done = d.ms; });\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => SN.hub.ghosts.delete(id));\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (!SN.hub.reported) { SN.hub.reported = true; AIHub.result({ score: Math.round(myShip().p / 16) }); } });\n  AIHub.on('end', e => { SN.hub.ended = true; SN.hub.endInfo = e; SN.audio.stopAll(); });\n  game.go('loading', { next: 'session', track: ev.track, then: () => AIHub.ready() });   // ready() once the world is warm\n}\n// in the session scene's update: card UI until started; countdown from AIHub.time(); race.step only when time() >= 0 and !ended;\n// every 100 ms: AIHub.send({ t: 'g', p, u, h, y, r, v, lap, fin }, { reliable: false }); every 1000 ms: AIHub.progress({ score, label });\n// on finish: AIHub.result({ time: Math.round(AIHub.time()), stats, awards }); AIHub.send({ t: 'done', ms }); SN.hub.reported = true\n```\n\n## Appendix E: World3D facts learned in planning (saves the builders an afternoon)\n\n- The 3D add-on is an ES module that imports `three/webgpu`, `three/tsl` and `@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat` by bare\n  specifier. It needs an import map. It attaches `E.World3D`, `E.THREE`, `E.TSL` and `E.RAPIER`, and throws if the 2D\n  engine isn't loaded first.\n- `await E.World3D.init(game)` creates one renderer for the page: WebGPU, else WebGL 2 (`?backend=webgl` forces it).\n  It makes `#view` under `#screen` if missing. The game must use `bg: null`. It always initialises Rapier (so Rapier\n  must be loadable even though craft don't use it). Headless it returns at once.\n- `new E.World3D(game, { terrain | level, sky, fog, ambient, sun, lights, glowLights, shadows, filter, camera,\n  onDraw, overlay })`.\n  - `terrain` coordinates run from 0 to `size` (a power-of-two chunk count): keep tracks inside (hence `origin`).\n  - `world.scene` takes your own three.js meshes. Use **node materials only**: MeshLambert / MeshToon / MeshBasic\n    NodeMaterial. Never ShaderMaterial, WebGLRenderer or addons.\n  - Make the materials at world creation. `world.prepare()` builds the shaders. `world.dispose()` before making the\n    next world.\n- The camera has modes `view`, `chase`, `first`, `fly`, `fixed`, `zones` and `behind`. We use `fixed` with\n  `camera.fixed = { x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, fov }`. `camera.far` and `camera.near` are in units.\n  `world.addCamera(o)` plus `game.splitScreen(2)` makes a split screen (filters are off while split).\n  `world.project(x, y, z)` gives HUD pixels.\n- `world.step(dt)` in update and `world.draw(r)` in draw, then the HUD with `r.overlay`.\n- `game.particles.*` draw in 3D and land on `particles.ground`. World3D resets that every draw: see edit §2.7.5.\n- Its settings keys: `look3d`, `picture3d` (`pixels` | `balanced` | `full`), `shadows3d`, `filter3d` (`clean` |\n  `cel` | `pixel`). `filter.bloom` is a boolean in the world's `filter`.\n- Its own racing (`world.track`, `world.vehicle`, a Rapier ball) is **not** used. The craft need track-space physics\n  at Wipeout speeds (§3.2), and the tracks need tunnels, drops, gaps and overpasses that `world.track` doesn't model.\n","numLines":435,"startLine":1649,"totalLines":2083}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RfjmNUmBZVfJ3h8P26pRy5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
