{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019bQvhAjnX9p8xYUUGQx1U9","type":"tool_result","content":"59:  enter() {\n67:  update(dt) {\n82:  draw(r) {\n265:/* =============================================================================\n266: * 1. SETUP  units, helpers, collision groups, the page's renderer (World3D.init)\n267: * ============================================================================= */\n325: *  play captures it (pointer lock; Esc or a pause frees it), then each move turns the camera (camera.mouseLook false:\n326: *  never). Off while a session is recorded or replayed: the lock is not in its record, so the replay would turn apart */\n346:/* =============================================================================\n347: * 2. TEXTURES AND MATERIALS  everything drawn by code, pixel by pixel, baked into crisp (nearest) textures\n348: * ============================================================================= */\n367: *  units; o: the legend entry (its colors: base, dark, light, ...). Add your own: World3D.GROUND.lava = (x, y, o) => ... */\n381: *  [r, g, b] (side, line, top, hi, lo) and (x, y) is a pixel of a w x h texture that repeats every metre (16 pixels)\n382: *  across; h is the pixels it spans up (64: earth's grass lip sits at the top of four metres) */\n445: * outward on the screen (along its normal for round parts, away from the part's centre for boxes) */\n461: *  casts a shadow), then build(scene) */\n462:class Merger {\n464:  add(geo, at, mats, shadow = true) {\n478:  build(scene, own) {\n488:/* =============================================================================\n489: * 3. LEVEL  written as text, one character per floor tile (1 metre, 16 units); row 0 is the far (north) edge, y grows\n490: *    south, x east. What each character is comes from the legend (LEGEND below, then the level's own legend over it):\n491: *      { floor: h }                  walkable at height h (units; 0 the ground; a raised floor is solid down to the ground)\n492: *      { wall: h }                   a solid block h tall (cut low where it stands between a view camera and the hall)\n493: *      { pillar: h }                 each block of these tiles is one pillar: plinth, shaft and capital\n494: *      { stairs: 'n'|'s'|'e'|'w', from, floor }   stairs rising toward that side, from height `from` (0) to `floor`\n495: *      { platform: h, thick: 4 }     a slab in the air whose top is at h (walk under it); with pit: true, over nothing\n496: *      { pit: true }                 no floor: a body that falls in is lost (actor.fell)\n497: *      { torch: true }               a brazier on the floor, lit by the world's torch lights\n498: *      { mark: 'name' }              a spot to put things: world.marks.name -> [{ x, y, z, cx, cy }] (the tile's centre)\n499: *    and how it looks: ground ('flagstone' 'grass' 'dirt' 'sand' 'snow' 'planks' 'tiles' 'plain' 'water' 'lava', a key of\n500: *    World3D.GROUND, or a function (x, y) -> [r, g, b]) with its colors (base, dark, light, flower), side ('brick' 'block'\n501: *    'earth' 'planks' 'metal') with color (and top, line). A level's own ground, side and color are every tile's default.\n502: * ============================================================================= */\n509:class Level {\n510:  constructor(world, def) {\n557:  ground(x, y) {\n569:  floorAt(x, y, z = 1e9) {\n580:  rects(key) {\n594:  _pass() {\n612:  colliders(pw) {\n632:class Flow {\n636:  to(x, y) {\n659:  dir(x, y, out = [0, 0]) {\n674: *      per look, walls and pillars instanced (cut low or to stumps by the view camera), stairs, platforms, braziers ---- */\n863:/* =============================================================================\n864: * 3b. TERRAIN  an open world instead of a level: new E.World3D(game, { terrain: { size, height, color, ... } })\n865: *    The ground is the game's height function (x, y) -> z in engine units, sampled every `cell` units (32: 2 m) into\n866: *    chunks of `chunk` cells (32: 64 m square), each chunk sampled the first time anything asks about it, so a world\n867: *    kilometres across costs only where someone goes. The same samples make all three of what the ground is:\n868: *      physics  a Rapier heightfield per chunk, for the chunks within `physics` units of any actor (world.step streams\n869: *               them: the same moves stream the same colliders, so a run replays exactly)\n870: *      queries  world.ground, floorAt, topH (and terrain.normal, slope) read the same triangles Rapier collides with (each\n871: *               cell split from its north-west corner to its south-east), and world.ray marches the height out where\n872: *               no collider is made yet\n873: *      picture  a quadtree of meshes, 2 m cells near the camera, coarser with distance out to `far`, a few built a frame\n874: *               (world.draw streams them; a coarser one stands in until its finer ones are ready), skirts hiding the\n875: *               seams between sizes, vertex colors from the game's color(x, y, z, nz) and, where the slope is steep,\n876: *               rock in strata (rock: { colors, band }), with a fine speckle and a broad mottle over all of it\n877: *    Everything in one material, every mesh from one pool made with the world: streaming never builds a shader\n878: * ============================================================================= */\n880:class Terrain {\n881:  constructor(world, def) {\n895:  heights(cx, cy) {\n903:  sample(gx, gy) {\n908:  _corners(x, y, need) {\n916:  ground(x, y) {\n921:  normal(x, y, out = [0, 0, 1]) {\n938:  rayDist(x, y, z, dx, dy, dz, len) {\n953:  stream(world) {\n969:  _collider(pw, cx, cy) {\n983: *      mottle), a pool of meshes sharing one index, and the quadtree that picks which to draw ---- */\n1031: *  them, their colors from the game, and the skirts hanging below its edges */\n1060: *  ones (all of them when budget is Infinity: the first frame), show those and hide the rest */\n1100:class TerrainFlow { to() { return this; } dir() { return null; } distance(x, y) { return 1e9; } }\n1103:/* =============================================================================\n1104: * 4. PARTS DRAWN BY CODE  instanced batches of four shapes (tube, ball, box, cone) in a toon look with outlines, and\n1105: *    two that glow (glow, halo); a pen that draws with them in engine units. Puppets, things and anything a game draws\n1106: *    in 3D go through them, so thousands of parts cost a handful of draw calls\n1107: * ============================================================================= */\n1110: * mesh the frame before (a render uploads the geometry, then updates the nodes), so a slot past the last frame's count\n1111: * drew, for one frame, what it last held: zeros (on the overlay, whose camera is the origin, a screen of outline ink) or\n1112: * a part from frames ago. So each upload reaches the most slots ever drawn and some room past them, and a slot never\n1113: * drawn holds a part too far away and too small to see */\n1118:class Batch {\n1120:  grow(cap) {\n1135:  put(ax, ay, az, bx, by, bz, cx, cy, cz, tx, ty, tz, col) {\n1143:  tube(a, b, r, col) {\n1152:  box(a, b, across, w, t, col) {\n1159:  end(outlines) {\n1167: *  no shadows, untagged: the overlay draws straight to the screen after the filter) */\n1183: *  right side down): its columns are the frame's forward, right and up */\n1191: * the pen: draws shapes in engine units, in a frame you set with at(x, y, z, yaw, size) (yaw turns it about z, from +x\n1192: * toward +y). Colors are '#rrggbb'. world.pen in a draw (before world.draw(r)), and every thing's drawing, use it:\n1193: *   ball(x, y, z, rx, ry, rz, color)   a ball (an egg: three radii along the frame's x, y and z)\n1194: *   box(x, y, z, w, d, h, color, yaw)  a box centred at (x, y, z): w along x, d along y, h up, turned by yaw more\n1195: *   tube(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, r, color), cone(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, r, color) (base to tip)\n1196: *   bar(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, w, t, color)   a flat bar from one point to the other (a blade, a plank), w wide, t thick\n1197: *   slab(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, ax, ay, az, w, t, color)   the same, w wide along (ax, ay, az): any way it leans\n1198: *   glow(x, y, z, r, color), halo(x, y, z, r, color)   unlit: a glowing ball, and light that adds round it\n1199: */\n1200:class Pen {\n1205:  at(x = 0, y = 0, z = 0, yaw = 0, k = 1, pitch = 0, roll = 0) {\n1209:  _p(x, y, z, out) {\n1215:  _rot(B, rx, ry, rz, yaw, x, y, z, color) {\n1229:  bar(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, w, t, color = '#ffffff') {\n1235:  slab(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, ax, ay, az, w, t, color = '#ffffff') {\n1243:/* =============================================================================\n1244: * 5. THINGS  pickups and set dressing drawn by code with the pen: world.thing(kind, x, y, z, o). A thing has\n1245: *    { kind, x, y, z, yaw, spin (turns a second), bob (units it floats up and down), size, color, open (0..1: a chest's\n1246: *    lid, a door), on, visible, t (its own clock) }. Add a kind: World3D.THINGS.lamp = (pen, t) => pen.tube(...)...\n1247: *    (local units: z up from the thing's base, x its front)\n1248: * ============================================================================= */\n1254:  star(p, t) {\n1313:/* =============================================================================\n1314: * 5b. SHAPES  the 2D engine's shapes (docs/ASSETS.md: E.SHAPES ids, a store set's 'SET:id', or an entry) in 3D, from the\n1315: *     same resolved parts (E.shapeMesh): each kind (an entry with its params, mats and mirror) is one instanced mesh, all\n1316: *     of them in one toon material whose texture is an atlas of the materials' patterns (E.materialTile) at world scale,\n1317: *     so a new kind or placement builds no shader. A solid one gets a fixed collider from the box the 2D engine collides\n1318: *     with (E.shapeBox)\n1319: * ============================================================================= */\n1410:/* =============================================================================\n1411: * 6. CHARACTERS DRAWN  each rig as it stands (the game poses it; this only reads it), as a Puppet (3D parts on the\n1412: *    rig's joints, sized from its build and colored from its palette) or a Card (the 2D engine draws the rig, exactly as\n1413: *    in the 2D games, from the camera's own turn and tilt, onto a card standing where it is). Blobs (slimes) squash as\n1414: *    they do in 2D; orbs ({ color, r }) glow. A blob shadow lies on the surface under every body\n1415: * ============================================================================= */\n1537: *      mesh, made when first needed and kept; only the pages used upload each frame; every page compiles to the same\n1538: *      shader: each card's cell comes from a per-card attribute, and each page has room for over 1,000 cards (three\n1539: *      r182 keeps the matrices of an instanced mesh with 1,000 or fewer in a uniform buffer named after the mesh, which\n1540: *      makes every such mesh's shader its own) ---- */\n1611:/* =============================================================================\n1612: * 7. CAMERA  world.camera: every camera a real 3D one, its pose worked out in the game's fixed steps (so the controls\n1613: *    that read it play back the same), its picture placed when the world draws.\n1614: *      'view'   the 2D engine's views as 3D cameras following the target (camera.target: the first hero unless set), a\n1615: *               little ahead of its aim with the 2D camera's lag: game.view (V cycles it), game.yaw ([ ] turn it),\n1616: *               game.zoom (the wheel, a pinch, Settings: Camera zoom). proj 'persp' (a lens, camera.fov) or 'ortho'\n1617: *               (the 2D engine's flat projection); dist pulls it back. Walls between the level and the camera are cut\n1618: *               low, pillars between it and the target cut to stumps (camera.cut false keeps them)\n1619: *      'chase'  behind the target and above it: it swings round behind as the target moves (chase.auto), turns with\n1620: *               [ ], the mouse once a click captures it (Esc frees it); game.zoom pulls it in; it slides in front of\n1621: *               walls rather than through them\n1622: *      'first'  the target's eyes (its body isn't drawn), 'fly' a free camera the move stick flies (jump up, dash\n1623: *               down), 'fixed' stays where camera.fixed says ({ x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, fov }): a game that runs its\n1624: *               own camera (a shooter's eyes, its over-the-shoulder view) sets it every step\n1625: *      'zones'  Resident Evil's: the region the target is in gives the camera (camera.zones: a fixed one, one that turns\n1626: *               to follow, one that slides on a rail), a cut when it moves on, held back until it is `margin` units\n1627: *               into the next region (hysteresis: no flicking back and forth on a border)\n1628: *    camera.ground(move) -> the move stick turned to the ground ([x, y], W walks away from the camera); across a cut it\n1629: *    keeps the old camera's way while the stick is held the same way (no walking back out of a doorway);\n1630: *    camera.steer(actor, move, dt) -> the same, or tank controls (the player's setting: World3D.CONTROLS);\n1631: *    camera.lock(from, target | list) -> lock-on (Zelda's targeting): the chase and first cameras turn to frame both,\n1632: *    ground() strafes round the target, a reticle marks it; cycle(list) the next in sight, unlock();\n1633: *    camera.aim(actor) -> the angle the mouse (on the floor) or right stick points from it, or null;\n1634: *    camera.heading: the ground angle it looks along; camera.pose: { x, y, z, yaw, pitch, fov, ortho } now\n1635: * ============================================================================= */\n1638:class Camera3D {\n1640:  constructor(world, o = {}) {\n1677:  set(mode) {\n1698:  update(dt) {\n1711:  _cutNow() {\n1716:  _zoneAt(x, y) {\n1721:  _zonePose(dt, t) {\n1741:  _behindPose(dt, t) {\n1754:  _passPose(P) {\n1758:  _viewPose(dt, t) {\n1769:  _chasePose(dt, t) {\n1783:  _firstPose(dt, t) {\n1790:  _flyPose(dt) {\n1801:  ground(mv, out = [0, 0]) {\n1816:  steer(a, mv, dt, out = [0, 0], o = {}) {\n1826:  lock(from, target, o = {}) {\n1834:  sight(from, a, range = this.lockRange) {\n1839:  pick(from, list) {\n1846:  cycle(list, dir = 1) {\n1854:  aim(a) {\n1862:  place(w, h) {\n1891:  cardView() {\n1899:/* =============================================================================\n1900: * 8. ACTORS  world.hero(o): a kinematic capsule that Rapier's character controller walks (it slides along walls,\n1901: *    climbs stairs and slopes, steps up curbs, jumps, rides moving platforms, pushes crates and shoves mobs aside);\n1902: *    world.mob(o): a dynamic body (a capsule, or a ball for blobs and orbs) that the crowd's own physics resolves.\n1903: *    Either way the game sets what it wants each step (vx, vy: ground velocity in units a second; jump(v) or vz) and\n1904: *    world.step moves it and reads back where it is.\n1905: * ============================================================================= */\n1906:class Actor {\n1908:  constructor(world, kind, o) {\n1924:  place(x, y, z) {\n1936:  setSolid(on) {\n1944:  resize(half) {\n1956:/* =============================================================================\n1957: * 8b. VEHICLES AND FLYERS  world.vehicle(o): a kart, a car or a hovercraft, a ball that Rapier rolls (walls, bumps,\n1958: *     ramps, jumps, falls) steered by the drive module's arcade handling (E.Car's: speed along the heading, a slide that\n1959: *     grip takes away, a kart's hop into a drift that charges a boost, the ground's surface), so E.Race drives it as it\n1960: *     drives an E.Car. world.flyer(o): a ship's arcade flight (yaw, pitch, a bank, barrel rolls and loops, boost and\n1961: *     brake), free within bounds or on rails along a path, worked out in the steps\n1962: * ============================================================================= */\n1970:class Vehicle extends Actor {\n1972:  constructor(world, o) {\n1989:  update(dt, map, c = {}) {\n2023: *  tilt it is drawn at), the surface's tag, a bump (it lost speed it wanted) */\n2036: *  and a cabin) or a hovercraft (a hull on pods over a glowing cushion); the front wheels turn with its steering */\n2056:class Flyer {\n2058:  constructor(world, o) {\n2069:  _frame() {\n2075:  update(dt, c = {}) {\n2106:  seek(list, o = {}) {\n2117:  at(k = this.world.game.alpha) {\n2125:class Track {\n2127:  constructor(world, o) {\n2147:  _build() {\n2187:  _pads(pen, t) {\n2200:  where(x, y, z) {\n2206:  surface(x, y, z) {\n2214:/* =============================================================================\n2215: * 9. THE WORLD  new E.World3D(game, o) (after await E.World3D.init(game)): a level, its physics, its actors, props,\n2216: *    platforms and things, its lights, sky and camera. world.step(dt) in the game's update, world.draw(r) in its draw\n2217: * ============================================================================= */\n2219:class World3D {\n2220:  constructor(game, o = {}) {\n2282:  reset() {\n2310:  randomFloor(rnd, minDist = 0, fx = 0, fy = 0) {\n2323:  clear(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1) {\n2332:  ray(x, y, z, dx, dy, dz, len, o = {}) {\n2349:  block(o) {\n2360:  hero(o = {}) {\n2371:  mob(o = {}) {\n2384:  vehicle(o = {}) {\n2402:  _surfaceAt(x, y, z) {\n2408:  remove(x) {\n2418:  near(x, y, r, kind = null, z = null) {\n2430:  box(o) {\n2437:  _prop(kind, x, y, z, yaw, shape, upright = false, fixed = false, mass = .5) {\n2446:  knock(p, fx, fy, dv, up = 0) {\n2456:  platform(o) {\n2469:  _movePlatform(p, dt) {\n2487:  thing(kind, x, y, z, o = {}) {\n2494:  setSolid(t, on) {\n2505:  touching(a, kind = null) {\n2513:  reach(a, range = 14, kinds = null) {\n2527:  unlock(door, inv, o = {}) {\n2536:  through(door, a, o = {}) {\n2543:  _pass(dt) {\n2557:  shape(id, x, y, z, o = {}) {\n2571:  step(dt) {\n2594:  _moveHero(a, dt) {\n2611:  _readBack(dt) {\n2641:  _pose(a, dt) {\n2650:  hash(extra = []) {\n2668:/* =============================================================================","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4eed361-ef26-4b83-9819-20dffd5cdae7","uuid":"4e72995a-6421-4b7c-9f93-840f50356bda","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:47:38.647Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"59:  enter() {\n67:  update(dt) {\n82:  draw(r) {\n265:/* =============================================================================\n266: * 1. SETUP  units, helpers, collision groups, the page's renderer (World3D.init)\n267: * ============================================================================= */\n325: *  play captures it (pointer lock; Esc or a pause frees it), then each move turns the camera (camera.mouseLook false:\n326: *  never). Off while a session is recorded or replayed: the lock is not in its record, so the replay would turn apart */\n346:/* =============================================================================\n347: * 2. TEXTURES AND MATERIALS  everything drawn by code, pixel by pixel, baked into crisp (nearest) textures\n348: * ============================================================================= */\n367: *  units; o: the legend entry (its colors: base, dark, light, ...). Add your own: World3D.GROUND.lava = (x, y, o) => ... */\n381: *  [r, g, b] (side, line, top, hi, lo) and (x, y) is a pixel of a w x h texture that repeats every metre (16 pixels)\n382: *  across; h is the pixels it spans up (64: earth's grass lip sits at the top of four metres) */\n445: * outward on the screen (along its normal for round parts, away from the part's centre for boxes) */\n461: *  casts a shadow), then build(scene) */\n462:class Merger {\n464:  add(geo, at, mats, shadow = true) {\n478:  build(scene, own) {\n488:/* =============================================================================\n489: * 3. LEVEL  written as text, one character per floor tile (1 metre, 16 units); row 0 is the far (north) edge, y grows\n490: *    south, x east. What each character is comes from the legend (LEGEND below, then the level's own legend over it):\n491: *      { floor: h }                  walkable at height h (units; 0 the ground; a raised floor is solid down to the ground)\n492: *      { wall: h }                   a solid block h tall (cut low where it stands between a view camera and the hall)\n493: *      { pillar: h }                 each block of these tiles is one pillar: plinth, shaft and capital\n494: *      { stairs: 'n'|'s'|'e'|'w', from, floor }   stairs rising toward that side, from height `from` (0) to `floor`\n495: *      { platform: h, thick: 4 }     a slab in the air whose top is at h (walk under it); with pit: true, over nothing\n496: *      { pit: true }                 no floor: a body that falls in is lost (actor.fell)\n497: *      { torch: true }               a brazier on the floor, lit by the world's torch lights\n498: *      { mark: 'name' }              a spot to put things: world.marks.name -> [{ x, y, z, cx, cy }] (the tile's centre)\n499: *    and how it looks: ground ('flagstone' 'grass' 'dirt' 'sand' 'snow' 'planks' 'tiles' 'plain' 'water' 'lava', a key of\n500: *    World3D.GROUND, or a function (x, y) -> [r, g, b]) with its colors (base, dark, light, flower), side ('brick' 'block'\n501: *    'earth' 'planks' 'metal') with color (and top, line). A level's own ground, side and color are every tile's default.\n502: * ============================================================================= */\n509:class Level {\n510:  constructor(world, def) {\n557:  ground(x, y) {\n569:  floorAt(x, y, z = 1e9) {\n580:  rects(key) {\n594:  _pass() {\n612:  colliders(pw) {\n632:class Flow {\n636:  to(x, y) {\n659:  dir(x, y, out = [0, 0]) {\n674: *      per look, walls and pillars instanced (cut low or to stumps by the view camera), stairs, platforms, braziers ---- */\n863:/* =============================================================================\n864: * 3b. TERRAIN  an open world instead of a level: new E.World3D(game, { terrain: { size, height, color, ... } })\n865: *    The ground is the game's height function (x, y) -> z in engine units, sampled every `cell` units (32: 2 m) into\n866: *    chunks of `chunk` cells (32: 64 m square), each chunk sampled the first time anything asks about it, so a world\n867: *    kilometres across costs only where someone goes. The same samples make all three of what the ground is:\n868: *      physics  a Rapier heightfield per chunk, for the chunks within `physics` units of any actor (world.step streams\n869: *               them: the same moves stream the same colliders, so a run replays exactly)\n870: *      queries  world.ground, floorAt, topH (and terrain.normal, slope) read the same triangles Rapier collides with (each\n871: *               cell split from its north-west corner to its south-east), and world.ray marches the height out where\n872: *               no collider is made yet\n873: *      picture  a quadtree of meshes, 2 m cells near the camera, coarser with distance out to `far`, a few built a frame\n874: *               (world.draw streams them; a coarser one stands in until its finer ones are ready), skirts hiding the\n875: *               seams between sizes, vertex colors from the game's color(x, y, z, nz) and, where the slope is steep,\n876: *               rock in strata (rock: { colors, band }), with a fine speckle and a broad mottle over all of it\n877: *    Everything in one material, every mesh from one pool made with the world: streaming never builds a shader\n878: * ============================================================================= */\n880:class Terrain {\n881:  constructor(world, def) {\n895:  heights(cx, cy) {\n903:  sample(gx, gy) {\n908:  _corners(x, y, need) {\n916:  ground(x, y) {\n921:  normal(x, y, out = [0, 0, 1]) {\n938:  rayDist(x, y, z, dx, dy, dz, len) {\n953:  stream(world) {\n969:  _collider(pw, cx, cy) {\n983: *      mottle), a pool of meshes sharing one index, and the quadtree that picks which to draw ---- */\n1031: *  them, their colors from the game, and the skirts hanging below its edges */\n1060: *  ones (all of them when budget is Infinity: the first frame), show those and hide the rest */\n1100:class TerrainFlow { to() { return this; } dir() { return null; } distance(x, y) { return 1e9; } }\n1103:/* =============================================================================\n1104: * 4. PARTS DRAWN BY CODE  instanced batches of four shapes (tube, ball, box, cone) in a toon look with outlines, and\n1105: *    two that glow (glow, halo); a pen that draws with them in engine units. Puppets, things and anything a game draws\n1106: *    in 3D go through them, so thousands of parts cost a handful of draw calls\n1107: * ============================================================================= */\n1110: * mesh the frame before (a render uploads the geometry, then updates the nodes), so a slot past the last frame's count\n1111: * drew, for one frame, what it last held: zeros (on the overlay, whose camera is the origin, a screen of outline ink) or\n1112: * a part from frames ago. So each upload reaches the most slots ever drawn and some room past them, and a slot never\n1113: * drawn holds a part too far away and too small to see */\n1118:class Batch {\n1120:  grow(cap) {\n1135:  put(ax, ay, az, bx, by, bz, cx, cy, cz, tx, ty, tz, col) {\n1143:  tube(a, b, r, col) {\n1152:  box(a, b, across, w, t, col) {\n1159:  end(outlines) {\n1167: *  no shadows, untagged: the overlay draws straight to the screen after the filter) */\n1183: *  right side down): its columns are the frame's forward, right and up */\n1191: * the pen: draws shapes in engine units, in a frame you set with at(x, y, z, yaw, size) (yaw turns it about z, from +x\n1192: * toward +y). Colors are '#rrggbb'. world.pen in a draw (before world.draw(r)), and every thing's drawing, use it:\n1193: *   ball(x, y, z, rx, ry, rz, color)   a ball (an egg: three radii along the frame's x, y and z)\n1194: *   box(x, y, z, w, d, h, color, yaw)  a box centred at (x, y, z): w along x, d along y, h up, turned by yaw more\n1195: *   tube(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, r, color), cone(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, r, color) (base to tip)\n1196: *   bar(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, w, t, color)   a flat bar from one point to the other (a blade, a plank), w wide, t thick\n1197: *   slab(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, ax, ay, az, w, t, color)   the same, w wide along (ax, ay, az): any way it leans\n1198: *   glow(x, y, z, r, color), halo(x, y, z, r, color)   unlit: a glowing ball, and light that adds round it\n1199: */\n1200:class Pen {\n1205:  at(x = 0, y = 0, z = 0, yaw = 0, k = 1, pitch = 0, roll = 0) {\n1209:  _p(x, y, z, out) {\n1215:  _rot(B, rx, ry, rz, yaw, x, y, z, color) {\n1229:  bar(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, w, t, color = '#ffffff') {\n1235:  slab(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, ax, ay, az, w, t, color = '#ffffff') {\n1243:/* =============================================================================\n1244: * 5. THINGS  pickups and set dressing drawn by code with the pen: world.thing(kind, x, y, z, o). A thing has\n1245: *    { kind, x, y, z, yaw, spin (turns a second), bob (units it floats up and down), size, color, open (0..1: a chest's\n1246: *    lid, a door), on, visible, t (its own clock) }. Add a kind: World3D.THINGS.lamp = (pen, t) => pen.tube(...)...\n1247: *    (local units: z up from the thing's base, x its front)\n1248: * ============================================================================= */\n1254:  star(p, t) {\n1313:/* =============================================================================\n1314: * 5b. SHAPES  the 2D engine's shapes (docs/ASSETS.md: E.SHAPES ids, a store set's 'SET:id', or an entry) in 3D, from the\n1315: *     same resolved parts (E.shapeMesh): each kind (an entry with its params, mats and mirror) is one instanced mesh, all\n1316: *     of them in one toon material whose texture is an atlas of the materials' patterns (E.materialTile) at world scale,\n1317: *     so a new kind or placement builds no shader. A solid one gets a fixed collider from the box the 2D engine collides\n1318: *     with (E.shapeBox)\n1319: * ============================================================================= */\n1410:/* =============================================================================\n1411: * 6. CHARACTERS DRAWN  each rig as it stands (the game poses it; this only reads it), as a Puppet (3D parts on the\n1412: *    rig's joints, sized from its build and colored from its palette) or a Card (the 2D engine draws the rig, exactly as\n1413: *    in the 2D games, from the camera's own turn and tilt, onto a card standing where it is). Blobs (slimes) squash as\n1414: *    they do in 2D; orbs ({ color, r }) glow. A blob shadow lies on the surface under every body\n1415: * ============================================================================= */\n1537: *      mesh, made when first needed and kept; only the pages used upload each frame; every page compiles to the same\n1538: *      shader: each card's cell comes from a per-card attribute, and each page has room for over 1,000 cards (three\n1539: *      r182 keeps the matrices of an instanced mesh with 1,000 or fewer in a uniform buffer named after the mesh, which\n1540: *      makes every such mesh's shader its own) ---- */\n1611:/* =============================================================================\n1612: * 7. CAMERA  world.camera: every camera a real 3D one, its pose worked out in the game's fixed steps (so the controls\n1613: *    that read it play back the same), its picture placed when the world draws.\n1614: *      'view'   the 2D engine's views as 3D cameras following the target (camera.target: the first hero unless set), a\n1615: *               little ahead of its aim with the 2D camera's lag: game.view (V cycles it), game.yaw ([ ] turn it),\n1616: *               game.zoom (the wheel, a pinch, Settings: Camera zoom). proj 'persp' (a lens, camera.fov) or 'ortho'\n1617: *               (the 2D engine's flat projection); dist pulls it back. Walls between the level and the camera are cut\n1618: *               low, pillars between it and the target cut to stumps (camera.cut false keeps them)\n1619: *      'chase'  behind the target and above it: it swings round behind as the target moves (chase.auto), turns with\n1620: *               [ ], the mouse once a click captures it (Esc frees it); game.zoom pulls it in; it slides in front of\n1621: *               walls rather than through them\n1622: *      'first'  the target's eyes (its body isn't drawn), 'fly' a free camera the move stick flies (jump up, dash\n1623: *               down), 'fixed' stays where camera.fixed says ({ x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, fov }): a game that runs its\n1624: *               own camera (a shooter's eyes, its over-the-shoulder view) sets it every step\n1625: *      'zones'  Resident Evil's: the region the target is in gives the camera (camera.zones: a fixed one, one that turns\n1626: *               to follow, one that slides on a rail), a cut when it moves on, held back until it is `margin` units\n1627: *               into the next region (hysteresis: no flicking back and forth on a border)\n1628: *    camera.ground(move) -> the move stick turned to the ground ([x, y], W walks away from the camera); across a cut it\n1629: *    keeps the old camera's way while the stick is held the same way (no walking back out of a doorway);\n1630: *    camera.steer(actor, move, dt) -> the same, or tank controls (the player's setting: World3D.CONTROLS);\n1631: *    camera.lock(from, target | list) -> lock-on (Zelda's targeting): the chase and first cameras turn to frame both,\n1632: *    ground() strafes round the target, a reticle marks it; cycle(list) the next in sight, unlock();\n1633: *    camera.aim(actor) -> the angle the mouse (on the floor) or right stick points from it, or null;\n1634: *    camera.heading: the ground angle it looks along; camera.pose: { x, y, z, yaw, pitch, fov, ortho } now\n1635: * ============================================================================= */\n1638:class Camera3D {\n1640:  constructor(world, o = {}) {\n1677:  set(mode) {\n1698:  update(dt) {\n1711:  _cutNow() {\n1716:  _zoneAt(x, y) {\n1721:  _zonePose(dt, t) {\n1741:  _behindPose(dt, t) {\n1754:  _passPose(P) {\n1758:  _viewPose(dt, t) {\n1769:  _chasePose(dt, t) {\n1783:  _firstPose(dt, t) {\n1790:  _flyPose(dt) {\n1801:  ground(mv, out = [0, 0]) {\n1816:  steer(a, mv, dt, out = [0, 0], o = {}) {\n1826:  lock(from, target, o = {}) {\n1834:  sight(from, a, range = this.lockRange) {\n1839:  pick(from, list) {\n1846:  cycle(list, dir = 1) {\n1854:  aim(a) {\n1862:  place(w, h) {\n1891:  cardView() {\n1899:/* =============================================================================\n1900: * 8. ACTORS  world.hero(o): a kinematic capsule that Rapier's character controller walks (it slides along walls,\n1901: *    climbs stairs and slopes, steps up curbs, jumps, rides moving platforms, pushes crates and shoves mobs aside);\n1902: *    world.mob(o): a dynamic body (a capsule, or a ball for blobs and orbs) that the crowd's own physics resolves.\n1903: *    Either way the game sets what it wants each step (vx, vy: ground velocity in units a second; jump(v) or vz) and\n1904: *    world.step moves it and reads back where it is.\n1905: * ============================================================================= */\n1906:class Actor {\n1908:  constructor(world, kind, o) {\n1924:  place(x, y, z) {\n1936:  setSolid(on) {\n1944:  resize(half) {\n1956:/* =============================================================================\n1957: * 8b. VEHICLES AND FLYERS  world.vehicle(o): a kart, a car or a hovercraft, a ball that Rapier rolls (walls, bumps,\n1958: *     ramps, jumps, falls) steered by the drive module's arcade handling (E.Car's: speed along the heading, a slide that\n1959: *     grip takes away, a kart's hop into a drift that charges a boost, the ground's surface), so E.Race drives it as it\n1960: *     drives an E.Car. world.flyer(o): a ship's arcade flight (yaw, pitch, a bank, barrel rolls and loops, boost and\n1961: *     brake), free within bounds or on rails along a path, worked out in the steps\n1962: * ============================================================================= */\n1970:class Vehicle extends Actor {\n1972:  constructor(world, o) {\n1989:  update(dt, map, c = {}) {\n2023: *  tilt it is drawn at), the surface's tag, a bump (it lost speed it wanted) */\n2036: *  and a cabin) or a hovercraft (a hull on pods over a glowing cushion); the front wheels turn with its steering */\n2056:class Flyer {\n2058:  constructor(world, o) {\n2069:  _frame() {\n2075:  update(dt, c = {}) {\n2106:  seek(list, o = {}) {\n2117:  at(k = this.world.game.alpha) {\n2125:class Track {\n2127:  constructor(world, o) {\n2147:  _build() {\n2187:  _pads(pen, t) {\n2200:  where(x, y, z) {\n2206:  surface(x, y, z) {\n2214:/* =============================================================================\n2215: * 9. THE WORLD  new E.World3D(game, o) (after await E.World3D.init(game)): a level, its physics, its actors, props,\n2216: *    platforms and things, its lights, sky and camera. world.step(dt) in the game's update, world.draw(r) in its draw\n2217: * ============================================================================= */\n2219:class World3D {\n2220:  constructor(game, o = {}) {\n2282:  reset() {\n2310:  randomFloor(rnd, minDist = 0, fx = 0, fy = 0) {\n2323:  clear(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1) {\n2332:  ray(x, y, z, dx, dy, dz, len, o = {}) {\n2349:  block(o) {\n2360:  hero(o = {}) {\n2371:  mob(o = {}) {\n2384:  vehicle(o = {}) {\n2402:  _surfaceAt(x, y, z) {\n2408:  remove(x) {\n2418:  near(x, y, r, kind = null, z = null) {\n2430:  box(o) {\n2437:  _prop(kind, x, y, z, yaw, shape, upright = false, fixed = false, mass = .5) {\n2446:  knock(p, fx, fy, dv, up = 0) {\n2456:  platform(o) {\n2469:  _movePlatform(p, dt) {\n2487:  thing(kind, x, y, z, o = {}) {\n2494:  setSolid(t, on) {\n2505:  touching(a, kind = null) {\n2513:  reach(a, range = 14, kinds = null) {\n2527:  unlock(door, inv, o = {}) {\n2536:  through(door, a, o = {}) {\n2543:  _pass(dt) {\n2557:  shape(id, x, y, z, o = {}) {\n2571:  step(dt) {\n2594:  _moveHero(a, dt) {\n2611:  _readBack(dt) {\n2641:  _pose(a, dt) {\n2650:  hash(extra = []) {\n2668:/* =============================================================================","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[],"moreFiles":0,"unavailable":true}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019bQvhAjnX9p8xYUUGQx1U9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh3bMxkU21DSdrEL9Lzw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FKmAT9JEY45NxBr6Na3fPE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ..; sed -n 265,345p engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js; sed -n 2219,2310p engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js","description":"Read World3D init and constructor"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7520,"cache_read_input_tokens":167219,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7520},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4eed361-ef26-4b83-9819-20dffd5cdae7","uuid":"e18f4a21-8a01-40c4-b185-e79151affa17","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:47:40.505Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh3bMi81u4YDjNxXaWix","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01FKmAT9JEY45NxBr6Na3fPE":{"command":"cd ..; sed -n 265,345p engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js; sed -n 2219,2310p engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js","description":"Read World3D init and constructor"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FKmAT9JEY45NxBr6Na3fPE","type":"tool_result","content":"/* =============================================================================\n * 1. SETUP  units, helpers, collision groups, the page's renderer (World3D.init)\n * ============================================================================= */\nconst E = globalThis.My3D2dge;\nif (!E || !E.Game) throw new Error('my-3D2dge 3D: load the engine (engine/my-3d2dge.js, a classic script) before this module');\nconst { clamp, lerp, approach, TAU } = E;\n/** U: engine units per metre (one floor tile is 16 units: one metre). three.js works in metres with y up */\nconst U = 16, T = 16, DEG = Math.PI / 180, OUTLINE = '#0c0818';\nconst Z_UP = { x: Math.SQRT1_2, y: 0, z: 0, w: Math.SQRT1_2 };   // Rapier's capsules and cylinders stand along y: this stands them up along z\n/** engine units (x east, y south, z up) -> three.js metres (x east, y up, z south) */\nconst toThree = (x, y, z, out = new THREE.Vector3()) => out.set(x / U, z / U, y / U);\nconst _lin = new Map(), _col = new THREE.Color();\n/** '#rrggbb' -> linear RGB floats (cached): instance colors */\nfunction lin(hex) { let v = _lin.get(hex); if (!v) { _col.set(hex); v = [_col.r, _col.g, _col.b]; _lin.set(hex, v); } return v; }\nconst _F32 = new Float32Array(1), _I32 = new Uint32Array(_F32.buffer);\n/** a hash of a list of numbers by their exact float32 bits (FNV-1a), as 8 hex digits: equal state, equal hash */\nfunction hashNumbers(list) {\n  let h = 0x811c9dc5;\n  for (const n of list) { _F32[0] = n; h ^= _I32[0]; h = Math.imul(h, 0x01000193) >>> 0; }\n  return h.toString(16).padStart(8, '0');\n}\n// collision groups (Rapier: membership << 16 | filter; a pair touches when each one's filter has the other's membership):\n// the level and platforms touch everything; props everything but flyers; heroes the level, props, platforms and mobs\n// (their capsules shove mobs aside); mobs each other too; flyers the level and each other; the downed (setSolid(false))\n// the level, props and platforms only\nconst ig = (member, filter) => (member << 16) | filter;\nconst GROUPS = { level: ig(1, 0xffff), platform: ig(64, 0xffff), prop: ig(2, 1 | 2 | 4 | 8 | 32 | 64), hero: ig(4, 1 | 2 | 8 | 64),\n  mob: ig(8, 1 | 2 | 4 | 8 | 64), flyer: ig(16, 1 | 16 | 64), down: ig(32, 1 | 2 | 64) };\nconst HERO_QUERY = ig(4, 1 | 2 | 64);   // a hero's controller steers round the level, props and platforms; its capsule shoves monsters\nconst LEVEL_ONLY = ig(0xffff, 1 | 64);  // sight lines and camera checks: the level and platforms\n\n/** the page's one renderer and 3D canvas, shared by every world (World3D.init makes them) */\nconst PAGE = { ready: null, renderer: null, canvas: null, backend: 'none', game: null, worlds: new Set(), active: null };\nasync function init(game, o = {}) {\n  if (PAGE.ready) return PAGE.ready;\n  return (PAGE.ready = (async () => {\n    await RAPIER.init({});\n    PAGE.game = game;\n    if (o.render === false || !game || game.headless || typeof document === 'undefined') return PAGE;\n    // the 3D canvas: the page's #view, or one made right under the game's canvas, which stays on top (clear: bg null)\n    const gc = game.screen.canvas;\n    let cv = typeof o.canvas === 'string' ? document.getElementById(o.canvas) : o.canvas || document.getElementById('view');\n    if (!cv) { cv = document.createElement('canvas'); cv.id = 'view'; gc.parentNode.insertBefore(cv, gc); }\n    Object.assign(cv.style, { position: 'absolute', left: '0', top: '0', pointerEvents: 'none', zIndex: '0' });\n    if (!gc.style.zIndex) gc.style.zIndex = '1';\n    gc.style.background = 'transparent';\n    if (!game.screen.clear) E.warn('3d:bg', 'a 3D world draws under the game\\'s canvas: make the game with bg: null, or its background hides the world');\n    const qs = new URLSearchParams(location.search), webgl = o.backend === 'webgl' || qs.get('backend') === 'webgl';\n    const r = new THREE.WebGPURenderer({ canvas: cv, antialias: false, forceWebGL: webgl });\n    await r.init();\n    r.shadowMap.enabled = true; r.shadowMap.type = THREE.PCFShadowMap;\n    r.toneMapping = THREE.NoToneMapping; r.outputColorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace;\n    r.info.autoReset = false; r.setPixelRatio(1);\n    Object.assign(PAGE, { renderer: r, canvas: cv, backend: r.backend.isWebGPUBackend ? 'WebGPU' : 'WebGL 2' });\n    mouseLook(gc);\n    return PAGE;\n  })());\n}\n\n/** the mouse turns the chase, first-person and fly cameras of the world drawn last: a click on the game's canvas in\n *  play captures it (pointer lock; Esc or a pause frees it), then each move turns the camera (camera.mouseLook false:\n *  never). Off while a session is recorded or replayed: the lock is not in its record, so the replay would turn apart */\nfunction mouseLook(gc) {\n  const cam = () => { const w = PAGE.active; return w && w.camera; }, S = E.session;\n  gc.addEventListener('pointerdown', e => {\n    const c = cam(); if (!c || e.pointerType !== 'mouse' || !c.mouseLook || !(c.capture || ['chase', 'first', 'fly'].includes(c.mode)) || document.pointerLockElement) return;\n    if (PAGE.game.paused || (S && (S.recording || S.replaying))) return;\n    try { const r = gc.requestPointerLock(); if (r && r.catch) r.catch(() => {}); } catch (err) { /* refused: [ and ] still turn it */ }\n  });\n  document.addEventListener('pointerlockchange', () => { for (const w of PAGE.worlds) w.camera.locked = document.pointerLockElement === gc; });\n  document.addEventListener('mousemove', e => {\n    const c = cam(); if (!c || !c.locked || PAGE.game.paused) return;\n    const k = .0024, dx = e.movementX || 0, dy = e.movementY || 0;\n    if (c.capture) { c.mouse[0] += dx; c.mouse[1] += dy; return; }   // (the game turns its own camera with them)\n    c.yaw += dx * k; c._held = 1.5;\n    if (c.mode === 'chase') c.chase.pitch = clamp(c.chase.pitch - dy * k, -1.3, .15);\n    else if (c.mode === 'first') c.first.