iviera coast, red-rock desert, night megacity, arctic basin) and a neon-grid Overclock skin',\n    animation: 'The engine\\'s rigs (pilot cards and live portraits, podium poses cheer, wave and hips) and tweens; new procedural craft animation (bank and yaw roll, barrel rolls, hinged airbrake flaps, engine glow, exhaust and boost trails, shield flashes, explosions, the rescue drone), animated pads, turbines, Ferris wheel, lighthouse beam, aurora, traffic, weather',\n    audio: 'All synthesized in code: six original electronic songs built from chord progressions and patterns for the engine tracker (extended with filter envelopes, unison, pan, accents, claps, sub booms and sidechain), layered by race events; about 60 synthesized sound effects; engine hums with Doppler and pan; Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish voices for the announcer, pilots and principals',\n    online: 'AI Hub ghost-mode sessions (1 to 4 players race the same seeded event and see each other as ghosts); local 2-player split-screen Versus for the game on its own',\n    testing: 'Headless Node suites driving game.advance and game.debug (unit, physics, race, weapons, modes, flow, season, audio, hub mock) including a scripted playthrough of the whole game, plus Playwright browser checks of the bundle and screenshots; one command, failures only and a one-line count',\n    research: 'None beyond the plan; the engine docs and the AI Hub README were read',\n    environment: 'Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown',\n    model: 'Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium',\n    usage: 'unknown'\n  },\n  testingFeedback: [\n    'unknown',\n    'unknown',\n    'unknown',\n    'unknown'\n  ],\n  engineFeedback: [\n    'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown'\n  ],\n  promptFeedback: [\n    'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown'\n  ],\n  engineChanges: [\n    'Button symbols default to PlayStation and the option moved to Settings > Display (PlayStation or Xbox), so prompts follow the brief',\n    'PlayStation symbols added to both pixel fonts, so input.label() results print in running text',\n    'Analog button values: input.value(action) reads pad button values, so L2/R2 airbrakes are analog',\n    'Synth extensions: lowpass filter envelopes, unison detune, pan and accents on tracker notes, clap and sub-boom drums, kick sidechain ducking, for the electronic soundtrack',\n    'World3D particle ground can be the game\\'s own function, so sparks and debris land on the track deck, not the terrain below'\n  ],\n  aiHub: {\n    name: 'Snipeout HD', tagline: 'Anti-gravity. Anti-everyone.',\n    description: 'An anti-gravity combat racer: thread banked neon tracks at 600 km/h, snipe rivals with ten weapons and survive Overclock. Season, time trials, split screen and AI Hub ghost races.',\n    type: 'Game', genre: 'Racing', source: 'Wipeout HD', series: 'Wipeout', players: '1–4',\n    controls: 'Stick or A/D steer · ✕ or W thrust · L2/R2 or Q/E airbrakes · □ or Space fire · ○ or Shift absorb',\n    tags: ['3d', 'racing', 'sci-fi', 'vehicles', 'arcade', 'versus']\n  },\n  credits: [\n    'SNIPEOUT HD. An original game inspired by Wipeout HD. Not affiliated with Sony Interactive Entertainment.',\n    'Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 and my-3D2dge 3D (MIT). three.js r182 (MIT). Rapier 0.19.3 (Apache-2.0). AI Hub session client 1.4.0.',\n    'All music, sound and voices synthesized in code. No image or sound files.',\n    'Built by Anthropic claude-opus-5-5 from PLAN.md.',\n    'The Hoverline Championship, its teams, pilots, principals, sponsors and recording artists are fictional.'\n  ]\n};\n})();\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MusnhCF9hXoLQx9QVNHyV3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh6W499q7KbNMDrYo1ev","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015sz15737TL1tEHmBsMuZtZ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-184648__xa320fb/work/SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-184648/src/76-pages.js","content":"// Paged screens (L1/R1, Q/E, the wheel or the arrow chips turn pages): How to play, Records, About / Credits\n(() => {\nconst E = My3D2dge, SN = globalThis.SN, px = E.px;\nconst T = (g, s, x, y, c = '#ffffff', o = {}) => E.font.text(g, s, x, y, c, Object.assign({ shadow: '#000', outline: false }, o));\n/** a paged screen: pages = [{ title, draw(g, x, y, w, h) }] */\nfunction paged(id, title, pages, o = {}) {\n  let k = 0;\n  const turn = d => { k = (k + d + pages().length) % pages().length; };\n  return { id, title, layout: 'custom', noShade: true, tabs: turn, prompts: [['tabL', ''], ['tabR', 'PAGE']].concat(o.prompts || []), back: o.back,\n    items: () => [{ id: 'page', label: '', rect: null, left: () => turn(-1), right: () => turn(1), pick: () => turn(1) }],\n    draw(g, r, ui) {\n      const P = pages(), pg = P[k], Wd = r.W, H = r.H, x = 16, y = 50, w = Wd - 32, h = H - 76;\n      E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg: ['#141a2ef0', '#05060cf0'], border: '#29c8e8' });\n      T(g, pg.title, x + 10, y + 8, '#29c8e8', { scale: 2 }); T(g, (k + 1) + '/' + P.length, x + w - 10, y + 10, '#9aa6c0', { align: 'right' });\n      pg.draw(g, x + 10, y + 30, w - 20, h - 40);\n      ui.items()[0].rect = [x, y, w, h];\n      const ay = y + h / 2 - 10; for (const [ax, d, s] of [[x - 14, -1, '<'], [x + w + 1, 1, '>']]) { px.rect(g, ax, ay, 13, 20, '#29c8e8'); px.rect(g, ax + 1, ay + 1, 11, 18, '#141a2e'); T(g, s, ax + 6, ay + 6, '#ffffff', { align: 'center' }); ui.chips.push([ax, ay, 13, 20, () => { turn(d); SN.sfx('ui_tab'); }]); }\n    } };\n}\nSN.paged = paged;\nconst para = (g, text, x, y, w, c = '#e8f0ff') => { const lines = E.font.wrap(text, w); lines.forEach((l, i) => T(g, l, x, y + i * 10, c)); return y + lines.length * 10 + 4; };\nconst keyRows = (g, rows, x, y, w) => { const I = SN.game.input; rows.forEach(([acts, label], i) => { let xx = x; for (const a of acts) xx += SN.glyph.draw(g, I, a, xx, y + i * 15) + 2; T(g, label, x + 70, y + i * 15 + 2, '#ffffff'); }); };\n/* ---- How to play: controls, racing, weapons (two pages), energy, modes ---- */\nSN.screens.howto = () => paged('howto', 'HOW TO PLAY', () => [\n  { title: 'CONTROLS', draw(g, x, y, w) { keyRows(g, [[['steer'], 'STEER'], [['pitch'], 'PITCH: NOSE DOWN / UP'], [['thrust'], 'THRUST (HOLD)'], [['brakeL', 'brakeR'], 'AIRBRAKES (ANALOG ON TRIGGERS)'], [['shiftL', 'shiftR'], 'SIDE-SHIFT / BARREL ROLL IN THE AIR'], [['fire'], 'FIRE (HOLD: CHARGE OR STREAM)'], [['absorb'], 'ABSORB WEAPON INTO SHIELD'], [['camera'], 'CAMERA'], [['lookBack'], 'LOOK BACK']], x, y, w); T(g, 'Prompts follow the device you touched last.', x, y + 140, '#9aa6c0', { font: 'tiny' }); } },\n  { title: 'RACING', draw(g, x, y, w) { let yy = para(g, 'Hold thrust. Steer into corners and squeeze the INSIDE airbrake: it works like a rudder and adds grip. Both airbrakes slow you down.', x, y, w); yy = para(g, 'Blue chevron pads boost you. Pitch the nose DOWN on descents for speed, UP over gaps to fly further.', x, yy, w); yy = para(g, 'Side-shift jumps four metres sideways. In the air, side-shift or flick the stick left-right for a BARREL ROLL: land it for a boost. It costs shield.', x, yy, w); para(g, 'Hold thrust in the countdown and release the rev bar in the green window at GO for a PERFECT START.', x, yy, w, '#ffd23f'); } },\n  { title: 'WEAPONS 1/2', draw(g, x, y, w) { SN.WEAPONS.slice(0, 5).forEach((wp, i) => { SN.drawWeaponIcon(g, wp.id, x, y + i * 28); T(g, wp.name, x + 30, y + i * 28 + 2, wp.color); E.font.text(g, wp.desc, x + 30, y + i * 28 + 12, '#e8f0ff', { wrap: w - 40, font: 'tiny', outline: false }); }); } },\n  { title: 'WEAPONS 2/2', draw(g, x, y, w) { SN.WEAPONS.slice(5).forEach((wp, i) => { SN.drawWeaponIcon(g, wp.id, x, y + i * 28); T(g, wp.name, x + 30, y + i * 28 + 2, wp.color); E.font.text(g, wp.desc, x + 30, y + i * 28 + 12, '#e8f0ff', { wrap: w - 40, font: 'tiny', outline: false }); }); } },\n  { title: 'ENERGY', draw(g, x, y, w) { let yy = para(g, 'Your SHIELD is your life. Walls, weapons, hard landings and barrel rolls drain it. At zero your craft is ELIMINATED.', x, y, w); yy = para(g, 'Ride the green PIT LANE strip to recharge. Or ABSORB a weapon you can\\'t use: it turns into shield.', x, yy, w); para(g, 'Fall off an open edge or into a gorge and the rescue drone puts you back, minus shield and time.', x, yy, w, '#ffd23f'); } },\n  { title: 'MODES', draw(g, x, y, w) { [['QUICK RACE', 'Eight craft, weapons on. Place counts.'], ['SEASON', 'Events, briefings, promotions, the Grand Prix.'], ['TIME TRIAL', 'Three laps against your own ghost.'], ['HOT LAP', 'A flying start. Your best lap counts.'], ['SNIPEOUT', 'Points for hits and eliminations.'], ['OVERCLOCK', 'Speed climbs every zone. Survive.'], ['VERSUS', 'Two players, split screen.'], ['ACADEMY', 'Eleven drills. Every mechanic.']].forEach(([a, b], i) => { T(g, a, x, y + i * 14, '#29c8e8'); T(g, b, x + 90, y + i * 14, '#e8f0ff'); }); } }\n]);\n/* ---- Records: one circuit per page ---- */\nSN.screens.records = () => paged('records', 'RECORDS', () => SN.TRACK_IDS.map(id => ({ title: SN.TRACKS[id].name, draw(g, x, y, w) {\n  const d = SN.save ? SN.save.data.records : {}; T(g, 'CLASS', x, y, '#9aa6c0'); T(g, 'RACE', x + 90, y, '#9aa6c0'); T(g, 'LAP', x + 170, y, '#9aa6c0'); T(g, 'TIME TRIAL', x + 240, y, '#9aa6c0');\n  SN.CLASSES.forEach((c, i) => { const yy = y + 16 + i * 16, r = d[id + '/' + c.id + '/race'], l = d[id + '/' + c.id + '/lap'], t = d[id + '/' + c.id + '/timetrial']; T(g, c.name, x, yy, '#ffffff'); T(g, r ? SN.fmtTime(r.ms / 1000) : '--', x + 90, yy); T(g, l ? SN.fmtTime(l.ms / 1000) : '--', x + 170, yy); T(g, t ? SN.fmtTime(t.ms / 1000) : '--', x + 240, yy); });\n  const z = d[id + '/zone']; T(g, 'OVERCLOCK BEST ZONE: ' + (z ? z.zone : '--'), x, y + 92, '#ff3ab4');\n  T(g, 'MEDAL TARGETS (TIME TRIAL / HOT LAP, GOLD)', x, y + 112, '#9aa6c0', { font: 'tiny' }); SN.CLASSES.forEach((c, i) => { const m = SN.medalTimes(id, c.id); T(g, c.name[0] + ' ' + SN.fmtTime(m.tt[0]) + ' / ' + SN.fmtTime(m.lap[0]), x + (i % 2) * 150, y + 124 + Math.floor(i / 2) * 10, '#ffd23f', { font: 'tiny' }); });\n} })));\n/* ---- About / Credits: source information, the three feedbacks, credits ---- */\nSN.screens.about = (o = {}) => {\n  const A = SN.ABOUT, si = A.sourceInformation;\n  const list = (items) => (g, x, y, w) => { let yy = y; for (const [k, v] of items) { if (yy > y + 150) break; T(g, k, x, yy, '#29c8e8', { font: 'tiny' }); const lines = E.font.wrap(String(v), w - 80, { font: 'tiny' }); lines.slice(0, 4).forEach((l, i) => T(g, l, x + 80, yy + i * 7, '#e8f0ff', { font: 'tiny' })); yy += Math.min(4, lines.length) * 7 + 3; } };\n  const qa = (qs, as) => (g, x, y, w) => { let yy = y; qs.forEach((q, i) => { T(g, q, x, yy, '#29c8e8', { font: 'tiny' }); const lines = E.font.wrap(String(as[i] || 'unknown'), w, { font: 'tiny' }); lines.slice(0, 5).forEach((l, j) => T(g, l, x, yy + 8 + j * 7, '#e8f0ff', { font: 'tiny' })); yy += 10 + Math.min(5, lines.length) * 7; }); };\n  const pages = [\n    { title: 'SOURCE INFORMATION', draw: list([['DATE', si.date], ['SOURCE', si.source], ['PLAN', si.plan], ['GENRE', si.genre], ['PERSPECTIVE', si.perspective], ['TECH', si.tech], ['ART', si.artDirection], ['ANIMATION', si.animation]]) },\n    { title: 'SOURCE INFORMATION 2', draw: list([['AUDIO', si.audio], ['ONLINE', si.online], ['TESTING', si.testing], ['RESEARCH', si.research], ['ENVIRONMENT', si.environment], ['MODEL', si.model], ['USAGE', si.usage]]) },\n    { title: 'TESTING FEEDBACK', draw: qa(['How many issues did testing catch?', 'How many were critical / game breaking?', 'Most helpful test?', 'Least helpful test?'], A.testingFeedback) },\n    { title: 'ENGINE FEEDBACK 1/2', draw: qa(['What did you like most about the engine?', 'Did you get stuck or guess wrong?', 'Most important thing you built yourself?'], A.engineFeedback.slice(0, 3)) },\n    { title: 'ENGINE FEEDBACK 2/2', draw: qa(['Hardest part about using the engine?', 'What did you change in the engine, and why?', 'One thing you would change?'], A.engineFeedback.slice(3)) },\n    { title: 'PROMPT FEEDBACK', draw: qa(['What did you like most about this prompt?', 'What was confusing?', 'What was the hardest thing to do?', 'What would you change?'], A.promptFeedback) },\n    { title: 'CREDITS', draw(g, x, y, w) { let yy = y; for (const c of A.credits) { yy = para(g, c, x, yy, w); } yy += 4; T(g, 'TEAMS', x, yy, '#29c8e8', { font: 'tiny' }); T(g, SN.TEAMS.map(t => t.name).join(' · '), x, yy + 8, '#e8f0ff', { font: 'tiny' }); T(g, 'ARTISTS', x, yy + 20, '#29c8e8', { font: 'tiny' }); T(g, Object.values(SN.SONGS).map(s => s.artist).join(' · '), x, yy + 28, '#e8f0ff', { font: 'tiny' }); T(g, 'ENGINE CHANGES', x, yy + 40, '#29c8e8', { font: 'tiny' }); A.engineChanges.forEach((c, i) => T(g, '- ' + c.slice(0, 90), x, yy + 48 + i * 7, '#9aa6c0', { font: 'tiny' })); } }\n  ];\n  if (o.credits) pages.unshift(pages.pop());\n  return paged('about', o.credits ? 'CREDITS' : 'ABOUT', () => pages, { back: o.credits ? () => { SN.UI.reset(SN.screens.main()); if (SN.hangar) SN.hangar.turntable(); } : undefined });\n};\n})();\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1514,"cache_read_input_tokens":519761,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1514},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4eed361-ef26-4b83-9819-20dffd5cdae7","uuid":"e3ceb0ec-c944-43b4-9ab7-3639d13cc4b3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:26:45.826Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh6W3t286zfZwYcYdft4","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_015sz15737TL1tEHmBsMuZtZ":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-184648__xa320fb/work/SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-184648/src/76-pages.js","content":"// Paged screens (L1/R1, Q/E, the wheel or the arrow chips turn pages): How to play, Records, About / Credits\n(() => {\nconst E = My3D2dge, SN = globalThis.SN, px = E.px;\nconst T = (g, s, x, y, c = '#ffffff', o = {}) => E.font.text(g, s, x, y, c, Object.assign({ shadow: '#000', outline: false }, o));\n/** a paged screen: pages = [{ title, draw(g, x, y, w, h) }] */\nfunction paged(id, title, pages, o = {}) {\n  let k = 0;\n  const turn = d => { k = (k + d + pages().length) % pages().length; };\n  return { id, title, layout: 'custom', noShade: true, tabs: turn, prompts: [['tabL', ''], ['tabR', 'PAGE']].concat(o.prompts || []), back: o.back,\n    items: () => [{ id: 'page', label: '', rect: null, left: () => turn(-1), right: () => turn(1), pick: () => turn(1) }],\n    draw(g, r, ui) {\n      const P = pages(), pg = P[k], Wd = r.W, H = r.H, x = 16, y = 50, w = Wd - 32, h = H - 76;\n      E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg: ['#141a2ef0', '#05060cf0'], border: '#29c8e8' });\n      T(g, pg.title, x + 10, y + 8, '#29c8e8', { scale: 2 }); T(g, (k + 1) + '/' + P.length, x + w - 10, y + 10, '#9aa6c0', { align: 'right' });\n      pg.draw(g, x + 10, y + 30, w - 20, h - 40);\n      ui.items()[0].rect = [x, y, w, h];\n      const ay = y + h / 2 - 10; for (const [ax, d, s] of [[x - 14, -1, '<'], [x + w + 1, 1, '>']]) { px.rect(g, ax, ay, 13, 20, '#29c8e8'); px.rect(g, ax + 1, ay + 1, 11, 18, '#141a2e'); T(g, s, ax + 6, ay + 6, '#ffffff', { align: 'center' }); ui.chips.push([ax, ay, 13, 20, () => { turn(d); SN.sfx('ui_tab'); }]); }\n    } };\n}\nSN.paged = paged;\nconst para = (g, text, x, y, w, c = '#e8f0ff') => { const lines = E.font.wrap(text, w); lines.forEach((l, i) => T(g, l, x, y + i * 10, c)); return y + lines.length * 10 + 4; };\nconst keyRows = (g, rows, x, y, w) => { const I = SN.game.input; rows.forEach(([acts, label], i) => { let xx = x; for (const a of acts) xx += SN.glyph.draw(g, I, a, xx, y + i * 15) + 2; T(g, label, x + 70, y + i * 15 + 2, '#ffffff'); }); };\n/* ---- How to play: controls, racing, weapons (two pages), energy, modes ---- */\nSN.screens.howto = () => paged('howto', 'HOW TO PLAY', () => [\n  { title: 'CONTROLS', draw(g, x, y, w) { keyRows(g, [[['steer'], 'STEER'], [['pitch'], 'PITCH: NOSE DOWN / UP'], [['thrust'], 'THRUST (HOLD)'], [['brakeL', 'brakeR'], 'AIRBRAKES (ANALOG ON TRIGGERS)'], [['shiftL', 'shiftR'], 'SIDE-SHIFT / BARREL ROLL IN THE AIR'], [['fire'], 'FIRE (HOLD: CHARGE OR STREAM)'], [['absorb'], 'ABSORB WEAPON INTO SHIELD'], [['camera'], 'CAMERA'], [['lookBack'], 'LOOK BACK']], x, y, w); T(g, 'Prompts follow the device you touched last.', x, y + 140, '#9aa6c0', { font: 'tiny' }); } },\n  { title: 'RACING', draw(g, x, y, w) { let yy = para(g, 'Hold thrust. Steer into corners and squeeze the INSIDE airbrake: it works like a rudder and adds grip. Both airbrakes slow you down.', x, y, w); yy = para(g, 'Blue chevron pads boost you. Pitch the nose DOWN on descents for speed, UP over gaps to fly further.', x, yy, w); yy = para(g, 'Side-shift jumps four metres sideways. In the air, side-shift or flick the stick left-right for a BARREL ROLL: land it for a boost. It costs shield.', x, yy, w); para(g, 'Hold thrust in the countdown and release the rev bar in the green window at GO for a PERFECT START.', x, yy, w, '#ffd23f'); } },\n  { title: 'WEAPONS 1/2', draw(g, x, y, w) { SN.WEAPONS.slice(0, 5).forEach((wp, i) => { SN.drawWeaponIcon(g, wp.id, x, y + i * 28); T(g, wp.name, x + 30, y + i * 28 + 2, wp.color); E.font.text(g, wp.desc, x + 30, y + i * 28 + 12, '#e8f0ff', { wrap: w - 40, font: 'tiny', outline: false }); }); } },\n  { title: 'WEAPONS 2/2', draw(g, x, y, w) { SN.WEAPONS.slice(5).forEach((wp, i) => { SN.drawWeaponIcon(g, wp.id, x, y + i * 28); T(g, wp.name, x + 30, y + i * 28 + 2, wp.color); E.font.text(g, wp.desc, x + 30, y + i * 28 + 12, '#e8f0ff', { wrap: w - 40, font: 'tiny', outline: false }); }); } },\n  { title: 'ENERGY', draw(g, x, y, w) { let yy = para(g, 'Your SHIELD is your life. Walls, weapons, hard landings and barrel rolls drain it. At zero your craft is ELIMINATED.', x, y, w); yy = para(g, 'Ride the green PIT LANE strip to recharge. Or ABSORB a weapon you can\\'t use: it turns into shield.', x, yy, w); para(g, 'Fall off an open edge or into a gorge and the rescue drone puts you back, minus shield and time.', x, yy, w, '#ffd23f'); } },\n  { title: 'MODES', draw(g, x, y, w) { [['QUICK RACE', 'Eight craft, weapons on. Place counts.'], ['SEASON', 'Events, briefings, promotions, the Grand Prix.'], ['TIME TRIAL', 'Three laps against your own ghost.'], ['HOT LAP', 'A flying start. Your best lap counts.'], ['SNIPEOUT', 'Points for hits and eliminations.'], ['OVERCLOCK', 'Speed climbs every zone. Survive.'], ['VERSUS', 'Two players, split screen.'], ['ACADEMY', 'Eleven drills. Every mechanic.']].forEach(([a, b], i) => { T(g, a, x, y + i * 14, '#29c8e8'); T(g, b, x + 90, y + i * 14, '#e8f0ff'); }); } }\n]);\n/* ---- Records: one circuit per page ---- */\nSN.screens.records = () => paged('records', 'RECORDS', () => SN.TRACK_IDS.map(id => ({ title: SN.TRACKS[id].name, draw(g, x, y, w) {\n  const d = SN.save ? SN.save.data.records : {}; T(g, 'CLASS', x, y, '#9aa6c0'); T(g, 'RACE', x + 90, y, '#9aa6c0'); T(g, 'LAP', x + 170, y, '#9aa6c0'); T(g, 'TIME TRIAL', x + 240, y, '#9aa6c0');\n  SN.CLASSES.forEach((c, i) => { const yy = y + 16 + i * 16, r = d[id + '/' + c.id + '/race'], l = d[id + '/' + c.id + '/lap'], t = d[id + '/' + c.id + '/timetrial']; T(g, c.name, x, yy, '#ffffff'); T(g, r ? SN.fmtTime(r.ms / 1000) : '--', x + 90, yy); T(g, l ? SN.fmtTime(l.ms / 1000) : '--', x + 170, yy); T(g, t ? SN.fmtTime(t.ms / 1000) : '--', x + 240, yy); });\n  const z = d[id + '/zone']; T(g, 'OVERCLOCK BEST ZONE: ' + (z ? z.zone : '--'), x, y + 92, '#ff3ab4');\n  T(g, 'MEDAL TARGETS (TIME TRIAL / HOT LAP, GOLD)', x, y + 112, '#9aa6c0', { font: 'tiny' }); SN.CLASSES.forEach((c, i) => { const m = SN.medalTimes(id, c.id); T(g, c.name[0] + ' ' + SN.fmtTime(m.tt[0]) + ' / ' + SN.fmtTime(m.lap[0]), x + (i % 2) * 150, y + 124 + Math.floor(i / 2) * 10, '#ffd23f', { font: 'tiny' }); });\n} })));\n/* ---- About / Credits: source information, the three feedbacks, credits ---- */\nSN.screens.about = (o = {}) => {\n  const A = SN.ABOUT, si = A.sourceInformation;\n  const list = (items) => (g, x, y, w) => { let yy = y; for (const [k, v] of items) { if (yy > y + 150) break; T(g, k, x, yy, '#29c8e8', { font: 'tiny' }); const lines = E.font.wrap(String(v), w - 80, { font: 'tiny' }); lines.slice(0, 4).forEach((l, i) => T(g, l, x + 80, yy + i * 7, '#e8f0ff', { font: 'tiny' })); yy += Math.min(4, lines.length) * 7 + 3; } };\n  const qa = (qs, as) => (g, x, y, w) => { let yy = y; qs.forEach((q, i) => { T(g, q, x, yy, '#29c8e8', { font: 'tiny' }); const lines = E.font.wrap(String(as[i] || 'unknown'), w, { font: 'tiny' }); lines.slice(0, 5).forEach((l, j) => T(g, l, x, yy + 8 + j * 7, '#e8f0ff', { font: 'tiny' })); yy += 10 + Math.min(5, lines.length) * 7; }); };\n  const pages = [\n    { title: 'SOURCE INFORMATION', draw: list([['DATE', si.date], ['SOURCE', si.source], ['PLAN', si.plan], ['GENRE', si.genre], ['PERSPECTIVE', si.perspective], ['TECH', si.tech], ['ART', si.artDirection], ['ANIMATION', si.animation]]) },\n    { title: 'SOURCE INFORMATION 2', draw: list([['AUDIO', si.audio], ['ONLINE', si.online], ['TESTING', si.testing], ['RESEARCH', si.research], ['ENVIRONMENT', si.environment], ['MODEL', si.model], ['USAGE', si.usage]]) },\n    { title: 'TESTING FEEDBACK', draw: qa(['How many issues did testing catch?', 'How many were critical / game breaking?', 'Most helpful test?', 'Least helpful test?'], A.testingFeedback) },\n    { title: 'ENGINE FEEDBACK 1/2', draw: qa(['What did you like most about the engine?', 'Did you get stuck or guess wrong?', 'Most important thing you built yourself?'], A.engineFeedback.slice(0, 3)) },\n    { title: 'ENGINE FEEDBACK 2/2', draw: qa(['Hardest part about using the engine?', 'What did you change in the engine, and why?', 'One thing you would change?'], A.engineFeedback.slice(3)) },\n    { title: 'PROMPT FEEDBACK', draw: qa(['What did you like most about this prompt?', 'What was confusing?', 'What was the hardest thing to do?', 'What would you change?'], A.promptFeedback) },\n    { title: 'CREDITS', draw(g, x, y, w) { let yy = y; for (const c of A.credits) { yy = para(g, c, x, yy, w); } yy += 4; T(g, 'TEAMS', x, yy, '#29c8e8', { font: 'tiny' }); T(g, SN.TEAMS.map(t => t.name).join(' · '), x, yy + 8, '#e8f0ff', { font: 'tiny' }); T(g, 'ARTISTS', x, yy + 20, '#29c8e8', { font: 'tiny' }); T(g, Object.values(SN.SONGS).map(s => s.artist).join(' · '), x, yy + 28, '#e8f0ff', { font: 'tiny' }); T(g, 'ENGINE CHANGES', x, yy + 40, '#29c8e8', { font: 'tiny' }); A.engineChanges.forEach((c, i) => T(g, '- ' + c.slice(0, 90), x, yy + 48 + i * 7, '#9aa6c0', { font: 'tiny' })); } }\n  ];\n  if (o.credits) pages.unshift(pages.pop());\n  return paged('about', o.credits ? 'CREDITS' : 'ABOUT', () => pages, { back: o.credits ? () => { SN.UI.reset(SN.screens.main()); if (SN.hangar) SN.hangar.turntable(); } : undefined });\n};\n})();\n"}}}
