{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh9TMvjrizGotB1ZoLXq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The engine's checker reports no errors, so I'm now writing the feedback answers into the About/exit-interview source.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1312,"cache_read_input_tokens":727700,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1312},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4eed361-ef26-4b83-9819-20dffd5cdae7","uuid":"57b867f6-0998-49e3-94c2-7676ee2aba85","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:04:43.966Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh9TMYvQqopjisdd2jtu","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":1,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh9TMvjrizGotB1ZoLXq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CqtfgKMQb9ixvv7BNKgQAU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-184648__xa320fb/work/SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-184648 && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/11-data-about.js'; s=open(p).read()\na=s.index(\"  testingFeedback: [\"); b=s.index(\"  engineChanges: [\")\nnew='''  testingFeedback: [\n    'About 27 real issues, caught by the headless suites, the bot-driven scripts and the screenshot reviews (plus a few bugs in the tests themselves). Examples: two scene fields named view and res that the engine silently treats as scene options, a crash entering the menu, replays drifting out of sync (quantised controls, the intro skip, a test bot sharing the autopilot\\\\'s AI state), the AI Hub round never calling ready() after a rename, craft popping up onto the far side of the gorge instead of crashing into it, the railshot missing at range, mouse hover not moving the focus, menu buttons losing their hit boxes, mirrored sign boards, and weapons eliminating five of eight craft a race.',\n    'About 7 were critical: the menu crash, the Academy crash on entry, the hub session never starting (ready() never called), replays desyncing (two separate causes), the team screen\\\\'s CONFIRM button not drawn or clickable, and unbound keys not leaving the attract mode.',\n    'The scripted playthrough of the whole game (attract, academy, all ten season events with briefings and promotions, the four-race Grand Prix, the ending, then every other mode, a replay and dev mode): it caught balance problems, drill limits and state leaking between modes that no unit test would. The AI Hub mock was a close second: it found the round that never started.',\n    'The pixel-brightness check of screenshots: it mostly flagged the deliberately black Overclock skin. Real visual problems (mirrored boards, the cluttered hangar, missing glyphs) were found by looking at the screenshots.'\n  ],\n  engineFeedback: [\n    'Everything around the game came for free and worked: fixed 1/120 s steps, headless game.advance for tests, the boot screen, pause menu, settings, key rebinding, saves, per-player input with half keyboards and split screen. World3D let me add my own three.js meshes and cameras under the same pixel HUD, fonts, dialog boxes and character portraits.',\n    'Yes. Scene objects\\\\' own fields named view and res are read as scene options (a warning, then wrong behaviour); game.go takes the fade as a third argument; mouse movement does not change input.lastDevice; the wheel is only reported where a scene allows zoom; text planes came out mirrored through the engine-to-three axis swap; and headless WebGPU (SwiftShader) loses its device, so browser tests run on ?backend=webgl.',\n    'Track-space hover physics on a banked spline ribbon (hover spring, grip cap, airbrakes, walls, gaps, drops, tunnels, overpasses), with the track mesh builder and the terrain carving around it. World3D\\\\'s own track and Rapier-ball vehicles cannot model Wipeout speeds, tunnels, drops, gaps or overpasses.',\n    'Coordinate conventions: the engine\\\\'s axes (x east, y south, z up) mapped to three.js by a reflection, which flips triangle winding, the camera roll sign and texture direction; I had to verify each by screenshot.',\n    'Five marked edits: PlayStation button symbols by default and the option moved to Display; PlayStation symbols in both pixel fonts; analog button values (input.value) for L2/R2 airbrakes; synth extensions (lowpass envelopes, unison, pan, accents, claps, sub booms, sidechain) for an electronic soundtrack; and a game-supplied particle ground in World3D so sparks land on the track deck.',\n    'A first-class ribbon track in World3D with track-space queries (s, u, h), arbitrary banking, tunnels, gaps and overpasses. Or, smaller: keep scene options in their own object so a scene\\\\'s game state can never collide with them.'\n  ],\n  promptFeedback: [\n    'The done criteria are concrete and testable: one file, no stubs, a dev mode with sliders, attract after 10 s, touch-only behaviour, controller-first prompts with an Xbox option, hub integration with a harness to prove it. The testing rules (one command, failures only, a one-line count) kept the feedback loop fast.',\n    'Where the 3D add-on stands: the brief says to build on dist/handoff, whose 2D views cannot show a banked, looping 3D track, while the add-on that can lives outside that folder. Also the plan was written for another run\\\\'s folder and file names, so TASK.md\\\\'s names had to override it.',\n    'The breadth in one pass: eleven modes, a season with a Grand Prix and an ending, the academy, attract, dev mode, split screen and AI Hub sessions, each tested, while judging a 3D picture only from screenshots.',\n    'Say how to weigh scope against polish when time is short, and name a reference screen size and refresh rate for the 10-foot UI. State plainly whether add-ons from the engine repository count as part of the engine.'\n  ],\n'''\ns=s[:a]+new+s[b:]\ns=s.replace(\"    research: 'None beyond the plan; the engine docs and the AI Hub README were read',\",\"    research: 'None beyond the plan: PLAN.md, the engine\\\\'s API card and the World3D header, and the AI Hub README',\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode --check src/11-data-about.js && node tools/exit-interview.mjs","description":"Write the final feedback answers; regenerate the exit interview"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1312,"cache_read_input_tokens":727700,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1312},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4eed361-ef26-4b83-9819-20dffd5cdae7","uuid":"61dcc43d-ea60-447b-bab3-3e6e7620d566","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:05:02.547Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh9TMYvQqopjisdd2jtu","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CqtfgKMQb9ixvv7BNKgQAU":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-184648__xa320fb/work/SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-184648 && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/11-data-about.js'; s=open(p).read()\na=s.index(\"  testingFeedback: [\"); b=s.index(\"  engineChanges: [\")\nnew='''  testingFeedback: [\n    'About 27 real issues, caught by the headless suites, the bot-driven scripts and the screenshot reviews (plus a few bugs in the tests themselves). Examples: two scene fields named view and res that the engine silently treats as scene options, a crash entering the menu, replays drifting out of sync (quantised controls, the intro skip, a test bot sharing the autopilot\\\\'s AI state), the AI Hub round never calling ready() after a rename, craft popping up onto the far side of the gorge instead of crashing into it, the railshot missing at range, mouse hover not moving the focus, menu buttons losing their hit boxes, mirrored sign boards, and weapons eliminating five of eight craft a race.',\n    'About 7 were critical: the menu crash, the Academy crash on entry, the hub session never starting (ready() never called), replays desyncing (two separate causes), the team screen\\\\'s CONFIRM button not drawn or clickable, and unbound keys not leaving the attract mode.',\n    'The scripted playthrough of the whole game (attract, academy, all ten season events with briefings and promotions, the four-race Grand Prix, the ending, then every other mode, a replay and dev mode): it caught balance problems, drill limits and state leaking between modes that no unit test would. The AI Hub mock was a close second: it found the round that never started.',\n    'The pixel-brightness check of screenshots: it mostly flagged the deliberately black Overclock skin. Real visual problems (mirrored boards, the cluttered hangar, missing glyphs) were found by looking at the screenshots.'\n  ],\n  engineFeedback: [\n    'Everything around the game came for free and worked: fixed 1/120 s steps, headless game.advance for tests, the boot screen, pause menu, settings, key rebinding, saves, per-player input with half keyboards and split screen. World3D let me add my own three.js meshes and cameras under the same pixel HUD, fonts, dialog boxes and character portraits.',\n    'Yes. Scene objects\\\\' own fields named view and res are read as scene options (a warning, then wrong behaviour); game.go takes the fade as a third argument; mouse movement does not change input.lastDevice; the wheel is only reported where a scene allows zoom; text planes came out mirrored through the engine-to-three axis swap; and headless WebGPU (SwiftShader) loses its device, so browser tests run on ?backend=webgl.',\n    'Track-space hover physics on a banked spline ribbon (hover spring, grip cap, airbrakes, walls, gaps, drops, tunnels, overpasses), with the track mesh builder and the terrain carving around it. World3D\\\\'s own track and Rapier-ball vehicles cannot model Wipeout speeds, tunnels, drops, gaps or overpasses.',\n    'Coordinate conventions: the engine\\\\'s axes (x east, y south, z up) mapped to three.js by a reflection, which flips triangle winding, the camera roll sign and texture direction; I had to verify each by screenshot.',\n    'Five marked edits: PlayStation button symbols by default and the option moved to Display; PlayStation symbols in both pixel fonts; analog button values (input.value) for L2/R2 airbrakes; synth extensions (lowpass envelopes, unison, pan, accents, claps, sub booms, sidechain) for an electronic soundtrack; and a game-supplied particle ground in World3D so sparks land on the track deck.',\n    'A first-class ribbon track in World3D with track-space queries (s, u, h), arbitrary banking, tunnels, gaps and overpasses. Or, smaller: keep scene options in their own object so a scene\\\\'s game state can never collide with them.'\n  ],\n  promptFeedback: [\n    'The done criteria are concrete and testable: one file, no stubs, a dev mode with sliders, attract after 10 s, touch-only behaviour, controller-first prompts with an Xbox option, hub integration with a harness to prove it. The testing rules (one command, failures only, a one-line count) kept the feedback loop fast.',\n    'Where the 3D add-on stands: the brief says to build on dist/handoff, whose 2D views cannot show a banked, looping 3D track, while the add-on that can lives outside that folder. Also the plan was written for another run\\\\'s folder and file names, so TASK.md\\\\'s names had to override it.',\n    'The breadth in one pass: eleven modes, a season with a Grand Prix and an ending, the academy, attract, dev mode, split screen and AI Hub sessions, each tested, while judging a 3D picture only from screenshots.',\n    'Say how to weigh scope against polish when time is short, and name a reference screen size and refresh rate for the 10-foot UI. State plainly whether add-ons from the engine repository count as part of the engine.'\n  ],\n'''\ns=s[:a]+new+s[b:]\ns=s.replace(\"    research: 'None beyond the plan; the engine docs and the AI Hub README were read',\",\"    research: 'None beyond the plan: PLAN.md, the engine\\\\'s API card and the World3D header, and the AI Hub README',\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode --check src/11-data-about.js && node tools/exit-interview.mjs","description":"Write the final feedback answers; regenerate the exit interview"}}}
