{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The bundled HTML exists in the root, exit-interview.json parses and fills every field, and the final reply has all four sections. But TASK.md asks for every feature to be implemented with no stubs or placeholders, and the transcript doesn't show that. The exit interview and About screen still contain 'unknown' values, the Testing, Engine and Prompt feedback sections are the agent's own assessments, and the Dev mode/attract/touch behaviours were only partly confirmed. The main gap is that the hub 'every copy says hello' check was not re-run after the final edits, and the one-line test count was read from a single full run whose result shows 'EXIT 0' only after later edits, so the completion claim is not fully supported."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4eed361-ef26-4b83-9819-20dffd5cdae7","uuid":"f62ec7e7-183d-4eee-8876-766ae04d2ed6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:17:33.684Z","isSynthetic":true}
