{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MpD853r9MMYgzNKp4sB8Y6","type":"tool_result","content":"exit-interview.json written and parses\nbundle: SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-184648.html 1.83 MB\n26/26 requirements pass\n467 passed, 0 failed (node 441, browser 22, hub 4) in 312 s\nEXIT 0\n[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: src/11-data-about.js. Call Read before editing.]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4eed361-ef26-4b83-9819-20dffd5cdae7","uuid":"634d413f-a651-4831-a6e4-40344f5748f2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:30:20.367Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"exit-interview.json written and parses\nbundle: SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-184648.html 1.83 MB\n26/26 requirements pass\n467 passed, 0 failed (node 441, browser 22, hub 4) in 312 s\nEXIT 0","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"staleReadFileStateHint":"[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: src/11-data-about.js. Call Read before editing.]"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MpD853r9MMYgzNKp4sB8Y6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghBRdaWNFKXXkATpgYgh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I checked every TASK.md requirement one by one against the final files, and all 26 pass. Then I reran the full test command after the very last edit: **467 passed, 0 failed** (441 headless, 22 browser, 4 hub), exit code 0. The hub's \"every copy says hello\" check passes in that same run, in all three harness scenarios.\n\nThe per-requirement check is a script, `tools/task-audit.mjs`, that drives the headless game directly:\n- **Single file:** the `.html` in the root, 1.9 MB, with no external script tags (three.js and Rapier load from the CDN, as TASK.md allows).\n- **Dev folder and engine:** all source, tests and tools are in the dev subfolder. The game is built on the handoff engine and its 3D add-on, with 11 marked edits.\n- **Title:** \"Snipeout HD\", picked by the plan's random draw.\n- **Nothing unfinished:** no TODO, FIXME, placeholder or stub in any of the 30 source files.\n- **Audio:** all made in code — 6 songs, 81 sound presets, and gibberish voices. No audio files.\n- **Modes played to their results screen:** race, time trial, hot lap, Snipeout and Overclock. The Academy passed 11/11 drills with no retries.\n- **Multiplayer:** 2-player split screen gives two viewports and two human craft. AI Hub tags and client are present, and the real harness passes.\n- **Replay:** a quick race replays to an identical end state.\n- **Season:** 10 events plus the Grand Prix and 39 story scripts. The separate playthrough test plays all of them, through the ending.\n- **Dev mode:** reached from the pause menu, 38 live sliders, and Reset All restores every default.\n- **Attract mode:** still on the title at 9.8 s idle, attract at 11 s. One loop shows all 10 weapons on all 4 tracks, and any input returns to the title.\n- **Controls:** PlayStation symbols by default, Xbox in Settings, and keyboard and mouse prompts. The triggers are analog.\n- **Touch-only devices:** the \"Controller or keyboard required\" notice with a settings button, no touch controls, and attract mode still runs.\n- **About/Credits and exit interview:** the game's About/Credits screen has all four sections, and `exit-interview.json` parses with every field answered.\n- **No runtime errors** during the audit.\n\nThe audit found one real bug, now fixed: the results screen offered REPLAY after the Academy. Drill resets move the craft outside the recorded simulation, so that replay would desync. REPLAY no longer appears there, and the audit checks it.\n\nTwo values stay \"unknown\" because I can't confirm them, which TASK.md allows: the browser, and the API cost and token counts. The usage line still gives an estimated session time. The feedback sections are my own assessments, because those questions ask for the builder's view.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:46:48\n- **Source:** Wipeout HD (Studio Liverpool / Sony Computer Entertainment, 2008)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** anti-gravity combat racing (arcade), plus a survival mode (Overclock) and a combat-points mode (Snipeout). Third-person chase camera (near and far), cockpit view and look-back. Trackside TV cameras for intros, spectating, replays and attract mode.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine (with marked edits) and the my-3D2dge 3D add-on v0.85.2 (World3D). three.js r182 (WebGPU, falling back to WebGL 2) and Rapier 0.19.3 from the jsDelivr CDN. AI Hub session client 1.4.0. Plain JavaScript. Node and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native style: pixel-resolution 3D with toon and lambert lighting, bloom, and the engine's pixel fonts and HUD. New procedural assets: six liveried craft designs, neon-walled banked tracks, tunnels, pads, gantries, sponsor boards, four themed worlds and a neon-grid Overclock skin.\n- **Animation:** the engine's rigs (pilot cards, live portraits, podium poses) and tweens. New procedural craft animation: banking, barrel rolls, airbrake flaps, engine glow, trails, shield flashes, explosions and the rescue drone. Animated scenery and weather.\n- **Audio:** six original electronic songs written as code for the engine's tracker, which I extended with filter envelopes, unison, pan, accents, claps, sub booms and sidechain. Layers come in at GO and on the final lap. About 60 synthesized sound effects, engine hums with Doppler and pan, and Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish for the announcer, pilots and team principals.\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost-mode sessions for 1–4 players, and local 2-player split-screen Versus.\n- **Testing:** headless Node suites using game.advance and game.debug (unit, physics, race, weapons, modes, flow, audio, hub mock, and a scripted playthrough of the whole game). Playwright browser checks of the single file. The real hub harness in 3 scenarios. One command, failures only, one-line count. Plus the per-requirement audit, `tools/task-audit.mjs`.\n- **Research:** none beyond PLAN.md, the engine's API card and World3D header, and the AI Hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** API cost unknown; tokens unknown (I can't see my own counters); session time about 1 h 35 min of wall clock.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 27 real issues, found by the headless suites, the bot-driven scripts and screenshot reviews. Examples:\n   - two scene fields named `view` and `res` that the engine silently treats as scene options\n   - a crash on entering the menu\n   - three separate causes of replays going out of sync\n   - the hub round never starting\n   - craft popping up onto the far side of the gorge instead of crashing into it\n   - the railshot missing at range\n   - mouse hover not moving the focus\n   - menu buttons losing their hit areas\n   - mirrored sign boards\n   - weapons eliminating five of eight craft per race\n   \n   The final audit then caught one more: REPLAY offered after the Academy.\n2. **How many were critical?** About 7:\n   - the menu crash\n   - the academy crash on entry\n   - the hub session never starting\n   - replay desyncs (two separate causes)\n   - the team screen's CONFIRM button missing and unclickable\n   - unbound keys not leaving attract mode\n3. **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough of the whole game. It caught balance problems, drill limits that were too tight, and state leaking between modes. The hub mock came second: it found the round that never started.\n4. **Least helpful test:** the screenshot brightness check. It mostly flagged the deliberately black Overclock skin. Real visual problems were found by looking at the screenshots.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** everything around the game came for free and worked: fixed time steps, headless testing with game.advance, the boot screen, pause menu, settings, key rebinding, saves, per-player input and split screen. World3D let me add my own three.js meshes and cameras under the same pixel HUD, fonts, dialogs and portraits.\n2. **Did I get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n   - scene fields named `view` and `res` are read as engine options\n   - `game.go` takes the fade as its third argument\n   - moving the mouse doesn't change `input.lastDevice`\n   - the mouse wheel is only reported where a scene allows zoom\n   - text came out mirrored because of the axis swap between the engine and three.js\n   - headless WebGPU loses its device, so browser tests need `?backend=webgl`\n3. **Most important thing I built myself:** hover physics that work in track space on a banked spline, with the track mesh builder and the terrain carving around it. World3D's own track and vehicle can't handle Wipeout speeds, tunnels, drops, gaps or overpasses.\n4. **Hardest part:** coordinate conventions. The engine's axes map to three.js by a mirror flip, which reverses triangle winding, the camera roll sign and text direction. I had to check each one with screenshots.\n5. **What I changed, and why:** five marked edits:\n   - PlayStation button symbols by default, with the option in Display settings\n   - PlayStation symbols added to both pixel fonts\n   - analog trigger values, for the airbrakes\n   - synth extensions, for an electronic soundtrack\n   - a game-supplied particle ground, so sparks land on the track deck\n6. **One thing I'd change:** a built-in ribbon track for World3D with track-relative queries, banking, tunnels, gaps and overpasses. Smaller alternative: keep scene options in their own object so they can't collide with a scene's own fields.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** the done criteria are concrete and testable, the hub harness proves the integration, and the one-command testing rule kept the feedback loop fast.\n2. **What was confusing:** the brief says to build on `dist/handoff`, but its 2D views can't show a banked 3D track, while the add-on that can lives outside that folder. The plan also used another run's folder and file names.\n3. **Hardest thing:** the breadth in one pass — eleven modes, a season, the academy, attract, dev mode, split screen and hub sessions, all tested — while judging 3D only from screenshots.\n4. **What I'd change:** say how to trade scope against polish when time is short, give a reference TV resolution, and say plainly whether engine add-ons count as part of the engine."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":618,"cache_read_input_tokens":762319,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":618},"output_tokens":750,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4eed361-ef26-4b83-9819-20dffd5cdae7","uuid":"1b81fa17-e3a9-4dcd-bdf9-deee7ad18084","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:30:45.881Z","request_id":"req_011CghBRbFcUcgdDwq8bPb3w"}
