{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: Several parts of the condition are supported by transcript evidence: the bundled single .html exists in the folder root, exit-interview.json was written and parses with all required fields filled, and the final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections. However, the condition requires every TASK.md feature to be implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, and the transcript evidence for full feature verification is incomplete. The per-requirement audit covers 26 items, and several items (Academy and season polish, Dev mode, attract mode and touch-only behaviour) are supported mainly by scripted tests and a limited set of screenshots rather than a complete item-by-item review. The reply also still reports two 'unknown' values (the browser and API cost/tokens), which TASK.md permits only for things that cannot be confirmed. The browser item is supplied as text by TASK.md, so its use there is defensible, but the 'unknown' allowance does not clearly extend to every field in the exit interview. The condition is therefore not clearly satisfied on transcript evidence alone."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4eed361-ef26-4b83-9819-20dffd5cdae7","uuid":"7f0bc452-ac61-4a39-9774-e821911d55cb","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:42:56.729Z","isSynthetic":true}
