er or keyboard required\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\n56:No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Na2Rf8AyyiF9uASq1hXZZv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghCuDjCtZBwsvoBXqgGp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I went through TASK.md line by line and recorded the evidence for each requirement from this session. The game files are as they were for the last checks: the per-requirement audit passed 26/26 and the full test command reported **467 passed, 0 failed**.\n\n| TASK.md line | Requirement | Status and evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| 3, 5 | Genre and perspective that fit the source | Anti-gravity combat racing. Chase, far-chase, cockpit and look-back cameras, plus trackside TV cameras. Screenshots of all four worlds, and of cockpit and chase views on Karakum's 28° banked spiral. |\n| 7 | Title picked by a real RNG | \"Snipeout HD\": PLAN.md's `secrets.randbelow(50)` draw, which STAGE.md says to use. It is in the `<title>` and on the title screen (audit). |\n| 9 | Research is my choice | Engine docs, World3D header and hub README only. |\n| 11 | Single HTML with the exact name; downloadable dependencies may be external | The file exists in the root with that name. Everything is inlined except three.js and Rapier from the CDN (audit, bundler checks). |\n| 13 | Build on the handoff engine; changes allowed | Engine v0.85.2 and its 3D add-on, with 11 marked edits listed in the About screen. |\n| 15, 17 | Native art and animation as the base, plus new assets and animations | Pixel-resolution World3D, pixel HUD and fonts, and engine rigs and portraits. New: six procedural craft, tracks, scenery, and craft and scenery animation. The screenshots were reviewed. |\n| 19 | All audio in code; gibberish voices | 6 songs and 81 sound presets, with no audio files. `SN.Voice` gibberish (audit, audio suite). |\n| 21, 44 | AI Hub integration, plus multiplayer on its own | Hub ghost mode passes the real harness in all 3 scenarios. Local 2-player Versus gives two viewports and two human craft (audit; a test drives it through the menus). |\n| 24 | Dev files in the subfolder, bundle in the root | Yes (audit). |\n| 26 | Performance budget unlimited | Full scenery, weather, lights, shadows and bloom. |\n| 28 | Headless tests with game.advance and game.debug, a whole-game playthrough, one command, failures only, one line | `tests/run.mjs`. The season suite plays attract, the Academy, E1–E10, the Grand Prix and ending, then every other mode. |\n| 38 | Feature-complete demo that captures the source | Races, time trial, hot lap, Snipeout and Overclock each reach their results screen. Academy 11/11 drills. The season covers 10 events, the Grand Prix and the ending, and replays reproduce exactly (audit and playthrough). |\n| 40 | Dev mode from the pause menu; live sliders with reset | Pause item \"Dev mode\", 38 sliders, and Reset All restores every default. Cheats are exercised in the flow suite. Screenshots of all four tabs and the overlay. |\n| 42 | Attract after 10 s idle, looping AI demo, any input exits | Still on the title at 9.8 s, attract at 11 s. One loop shows 10 weapons on 4 tracks, and a key, unbound key, pad or click exits (audit, browser test, screenshot). |\n| 46 | Narrative tone like the source | 39 scripts of clipped corporate race-control and team copy. A briefing was reviewed in a screenshot. |\n| 49 | 10-foot, controller-first; PS glyphs by default, Xbox option; native keyboard and mouse; prompts follow the last device | Glyphs ✕ ○ □ △ by default and A/B/X/Y via the setting. Analog L2 confirmed with a stubbed DualSense. Mouse hover and click work. Prompts switch with the device (browser and flow tests). |\n| 51 | No dense web-style screens | At most 6 tiles per screen in big type. The About text was split into short pages (screenshots). |\n| 53 | Touch-only: no touch controls, the notice and a settings button, attract runs | Confirmed on an emulated phone, with a screenshot (audit, browser test). |\n| 56 | No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | The source scan is clean, and the bundler refuses to build otherwise. |\n\n**On usage:** TASK.md asks for cost and tokens \"only if estimates are available.\" The figure I can actually estimate is output tokens: about 200K, based on the 0.48 MB of code and text I wrote. That is in the exit interview. Input tokens and dollar cost aren't visible to me. Presenting a number for them as a confirmed figure would mean making it up, so I'm stating plainly that it isn't available instead.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:46:48\n- **Source:** Wipeout HD (Studio Liverpool / Sony Computer Entertainment, 2008)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** anti-gravity combat racing (arcade), plus a survival mode (Overclock) and a combat-points mode (Snipeout). Third-person chase camera (near and far), cockpit view and look-back. Trackside TV cameras for intros, spectating, replays and attract mode.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine (with marked edits) and the my-3D2dge 3D add-on v0.85.2 (World3D). three.js r182 (WebGPU, falling back to WebGL 2) and Rapier 0.19.3 from the jsDelivr CDN. AI Hub session client 1.4.0. Plain JavaScript. Node and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native style: pixel-resolution 3D with toon and lambert lighting, bloom, and the engine's pixel fonts and HUD. New procedural assets: six liveried craft designs, neon-walled banked tracks, tunnels, pads, gantries, sponsor boards, four themed worlds and a neon-grid Overclock skin.\n- **Animation:** the engine's rigs (pilot cards, live portraits, podium poses) and tweens. New procedural craft animation: banking, barrel rolls, airbrake flaps, engine glow, trails, shield flashes, explosions and the rescue drone. Animated scenery and weather.\n- **Audio:** six original electronic songs written as code for the engine's tracker, which I extended with filter envelopes, unison, pan, accents, claps, sub booms and sidechain. Layers come in at GO and on the final lap. About 60 synthesized sound effects, engine hums with Doppler and pan, and Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish for the announcer, pilots and team principals.\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost-mode sessions for 1–4 players, and local 2-player split-screen Versus.\n- **Testing:** headless Node suites using game.advance and game.debug (unit, physics, race, weapons, modes, flow, audio, hub mock, and a scripted playthrough of the whole game). Playwright browser checks of the single file. The real hub harness in 3 scenarios. One command, failures only, one-line count. Plus the per-requirement audit (`tools/task-audit.mjs`) and screenshot reviews.\n- **Research:** none beyond PLAN.md, the engine's API card and World3D header, and the AI Hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser: headless Chromium build 1243 (Playwright 1.63.0, WebGL 2 backend) for every browser test and screenshot.\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** about 0.48 MB of code and tests written, which is roughly 140K output tokens for code and about 200K output tokens in all. Input tokens and API cost in USD weren't visible to me, so I haven't estimated them. Session time is about 2 h of wall clock (18:47 to 20:45 MST).\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 32 real issues, found by the headless suites, the bot-driven scripts, screenshot reviews and the final audit. Examples:\n   - two scene fields named `view` and `res` that the engine silently treats as scene options\n   - a crash on entering the menu\n   - replays going out of sync (three separate causes)\n   - the hub round never starting\n   - craft popping up onto the far side of the gorge instead of crashing into it\n   - the railshot missing at range\n   - mouse hover not moving the focus\n   - menu buttons losing their hit areas\n   - mirrored sign boards\n   - weapons eliminating five of eight craft per race\n   - REPLAY offered after the Academy\n   - four overlap problems found in the final screenshot review\n2. **How many were critical?** About 7:\n   - the menu crash\n   - the academy crash on entry\n   - the hub session never starting\n   - replay desyncs (two separate causes)\n   - the team screen's CONFIRM button missing and unclickable\n   - unbound keys not leaving attract mode\n3. **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough of the whole game. It caught balance problems, drill limits that were too tight, and state leaking between modes. The hub mock came second: it found the round that never started.\n4. **Least helpful test:** the screenshot brightness check. It mostly flagged the deliberately black Overclock skin. Real visual problems were found by looking at the screenshots.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** everything around the game came for free and worked: fixed time steps, headless testing with game.advance, the boot screen, pause menu, settings, key rebinding, saves, per-player input and split screen. World3D let me add my own three.js meshes and cameras under the same pixel HUD, fonts, dialogs and portraits.\n2. **Did I get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n   - scene fields named `view` and `res` are read as engine options\n   - `game.go` takes the fade as its third argument\n   - moving the mouse doesn't change `input.lastDevice`\n   - the mouse wheel is only reported where a scene allows zoom\n   - text came out mirrored because of the axis swap between the engine and three.js\n   - headless WebGPU loses its device, so browser tests need `?backend=webgl`\n3. **Most important thing I built myself:** hover physics that work in track space on a banked spline, with the track mesh builder and the terrain carving around it. World3D's own track and vehicle can't handle Wipeout speeds, tunnels, drops, gaps or overpasses.\n4. **Hardest part:** coordinate conventions. The engine's axes map to three.js by a mirror flip, which reverses triangle winding, the camera roll sign and text direction. I had to check each one with screenshots.\n5. **What I changed, and why:** five marked edits:\n   - PlayStation button symbols by default, with the option in Display settings\n   - PlayStation symbols added to both pixel fonts\n   - analog trigger values, for the airbrakes\n   - synth extensions, for an electronic soundtrack\n   - a game-supplied particle ground, so sparks land on the track deck\n6. **One thing I'd change:** a built-in ribbon track for World3D with track-relative queries, banking, tunnels, gaps and overpasses. Smaller alternative: keep scene options in their own object so they can't collide with a scene's own fields.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** the done criteria are concrete and testable, the hub harness proves the integration, and the one-command testing rule kept the feedback loop fast.\n2. **What was confusing:** the brief says to build on `dist/handoff`, but its 2D views can't show a banked 3D track, while the add-on that can lives outside that folder. The plan also used another run's folder and file names.\n3. **Hardest thing:** the breadth in one pass — eleven modes, a season, the academy, attract, dev mode, split screen and hub sessions, all tested — while judging 3D only from screenshots.\n4. **What I'd change:** say how to trade scope against polish when time is short, give a reference TV resolution, and say plainly whether engine add-ons count as part of the engine."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1665,"cache_read_input_tokens":804980,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1665},"output_tokens":777,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4eed361-ef26-4b83-9819-20dffd5cdae7","uuid":"71b0f66d-2657-4135-9e8b-905b43b69466","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:50:14.729Z","request_id":"req_011CghCuDQ7MeHpAA58tzLJH"}
