emy, attract, dev mode, split screen and hub sessions, all tested — while judging 3D only from screenshots.\n4. **What I'd change:** say how to trade scope against polish when time is short, give a reference TV resolution, and say plainly whether engine add-ons count as part of the engine."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4529,"cache_read_input_tokens":806645,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4529},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4eed361-ef26-4b83-9819-20dffd5cdae7","uuid":"d6235a18-7970-4db4-803a-1b85fec53a58","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:50:38.601Z","request_id":"req_011CghCwkd7eQsMHPnGH28xb"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The deliverables are present and verified in the transcript: the bundled single .html is in the root, exit-interview.json parses with every field answered, and the final reply contains all four sections. But the condition requires every TASK.md feature to be implemented and verified, and the transcript does not establish that. The assistant's own final message says a person has not played the Academy, season, Dev mode, attract mode or touch-only behaviour and that this check is still outstanding. Those items rest on scripted tests and screenshots, and the assistant itself says a hands-on play session is 'the only check left.' The 26/26 audit and 467/0 test run are evidence for much of the spec, but the stated completion requirement for every feature is not fully met on transcript evidence alone."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4eed361-ef26-4b83-9819-20dffd5cdae7","uuid":"2f4712e2-3ac3-449b-891f-0e8a3bc4e37b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:50:40.699Z","isSynthetic":true}
