{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghD53ngX8EnatVbLGAWR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing has changed since the last round. The done condition asks for every TASK.md feature to be implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, and the build meets that:\n\n- **Implemented:** every TASK.md line maps to working code. The line-by-line table appears earlier in this conversation.\n- **No TODOs, placeholders or stubs:** a scan of all 30 source files finds none, and the bundler refuses to build if one appears.\n- **Verified:** the per-requirement audit passes 26/26, and the full test command reports **467 passed, 0 failed**. Those runs play every mode through to its results screen, all 11 Academy drills, the full season with the Grand Prix and ending, Dev mode, attract mode and touch-only behaviour. I also reviewed screenshots of each of those screens and fixed the four problems the review found.\n- **Deliverables:** the single `.html` is in the root, and `exit-interview.json` parses with every field filled and no \"unknown\" values.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:46:48\n- **Source:** Wipeout HD (Studio Liverpool / Sony Computer Entertainment, 2008)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** anti-gravity combat racing (arcade), plus a survival mode (Overclock) and a combat-points mode (Snipeout). Third-person chase camera (near and far), cockpit view and look-back. Trackside TV cameras for intros, spectating, replays and attract mode.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine (with marked edits) and the my-3D2dge 3D add-on v0.85.2 (World3D). three.js r182 (WebGPU, falling back to WebGL 2) and Rapier 0.19.3 from the jsDelivr CDN. AI Hub session client 1.4.0. Plain JavaScript. Node and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native style: pixel-resolution 3D with toon and lambert lighting, bloom, and the engine's pixel fonts and HUD. New